.SH KOSHKA ARCHITECTURE AND CORE FEATURES
.SS Execution moods and option invariants
Koshka partitions shell behavior into four moods.
In this manual, \f[CR]bash\f[R] and \f[CR]bash\-posix\f[R] are referred
to as the \f[B]Bash moods\f[R], \f[CR]bash\-posix\f[R] and \f[CR]sh\f[R]
(where \f[CR]posix\f[R] is on) are the \f[B]POSIX moods\f[R], and
\f[CR]bash\f[R], \f[CR]bash\-posix\f[R], and \f[CR]sh\f[R] are the
\f[B]compatibility moods\f[R].
.PP
