T{
\f[CR]v\f[R], \f[CR]V\f[R], \f[CR]Ctrl\-V\f[R]
T}@T{
Enter character visual (\f[CR]v\f[R]), line visual (\f[CR]V\f[R]), or
rectangular block (\f[CR]Ctrl\-V\f[R]) selection.
Motions move the selection end (rectangle corner) and take no count.
Visual modes accept \f[CR]d\f[R]/\f[CR]x\f[R] (delete), \f[CR]c\f[R]
(change), \f[CR]y\f[R] (yank), \f[CR]gq\f[R] (wrap, repeatable with
\f[CR].\f[R]), and \f[CR]:\f[R] (colon commands on the selected lines,
shown as \f[CR]:\[aq]<,\[aq]>\f[R]); rectangle mode accepts
\f[CR]d\f[R]/\f[CR]x\f[R] and \f[CR]I\f[R]/\f[CR]c\f[R]/\f[CR]C\f[R]
(insert at the left column of every line when insert mode ends).
\f[CR]Escape\f[R], \f[CR]v\f[R] (visual modes), \f[CR]Ctrl\-V\f[R]
(rectangle mode), and unrecognized keys leave the selection;
\f[CR]Enter\f[R], \f[CR]Ctrl\-D\f[R], and \f[CR]Ctrl\-C\f[R] leave it
and behave as in Emacs mode.
