T{
Vi \f[CR]:\f[R] commands
T}@T{
\f[CR]Enter\f[R] runs the command, and \f[CR]Escape\f[R],
\f[CR]Ctrl\-C\f[R], \f[CR]Ctrl\-D\f[R], or \f[CR]Backspace\f[R] on an
empty line closes the prompt; unknown commands do nothing.
\f[CR]:q\f[R], \f[CR]:q!\f[R], \f[CR]:quit\f[R], \f[CR]:wq\f[R],
\f[CR]:wq!\f[R], \f[CR]:wqa\f[R], \f[CR]:wqa!\f[R], \f[CR]:x\f[R] (exit
with the status of the last command; in \f[CR]slurp\f[R], the
\f[CR]w\f[R] forms save first); \f[CR]:w\f[R], \f[CR]:write\f[R] (save
in \f[CR]slurp\f[R]); \f[CR]:N\f[R], \f[CR]:$\f[R] (jump to row
\f[CR]N\f[R] or end); \f[CR]:s/old/new/[g]\f[R] and
\f[CR]:%s/old/new/[g]\f[R] (replaces the first match of basic regular
expression \f[CR]old\f[R] on the caret row, or every match with
\f[CR]g\f[R]; \f[CR]:%s\f[R] acts on every row; any punctuation can
delimit; \f[CR]&\f[R] in \f[CR]new\f[R] is the match and
\f[CR]\[rs]1\f[R]\-\f[CR]\[rs]9\f[R] its groups; \f[CR]:&\f[R],
\f[CR]:&&\f[R] (keeps \f[CR]g\f[R]), and \f[CR]:s\f[R] repeat the last
substitution, and \f[CR]:%&\f[R] and \f[CR]:%&&\f[R] repeat it on every
row); \f[CR]:set option[=value|?]\f[R], \f[CR]:set nooption\f[R]
(mutate/query \f[CR]koshconf\f[R] with \f[CR]Tab\f[R] completion);
\f[CR]:save [option]\f[R] (writes the option, or every option, to
\f[CR]kosh.conf\f[R]); \f[CR]:format\f[R], \f[CR]:%format\f[R] (format
the caret row or the buffer as \f[CR]\-\-format\f[R] does; source that
does not parse stays unchanged and its error is shown); \f[CR]:e\f[R],
\f[CR]:edit\f[R] (edit in an external editor); \f[CR]:u\f[R],
\f[CR]:undo\f[R], \f[CR]:red\f[R], \f[CR]:redo\f[R]; \f[CR]:h\f[R],
\f[CR]:help\f[R] (list the colon commands until the next key).
T}
T{
Emacs \f[CR]M\-x\f[R] commands
T}@T{
\f[CR]Tab\f[R] completes a command, \f[CR]Enter\f[R] runs it, and
\f[CR]Escape\f[R], \f[CR]Ctrl\-C\f[R], \f[CR]Ctrl\-D\f[R], or
\f[CR]Backspace\f[R] on an empty minibuffer closes it.
Hint rows list the matching commands, with a description for each when
six or fewer match.
Commands: \f[CR]help\f[R] (list the commands),
\f[CR]replace\-string\f[R], \f[CR]replace\-regexp\f[R] (replace every
match in the buffer; supports \f[CR]\[rs]&\f[R] and
\f[CR]\[rs]1\f[R]\-\f[CR]\[rs]9\f[R]), \f[CR]repeat\f[R] (as
\f[CR]Ctrl\-X z\f[R]), \f[CR]set\-option\f[R], \f[CR]get\-option\f[R],
\f[CR]save\-option\f[R] (as \f[CR]:set\f[R] and \f[CR]:save\f[R]),
\f[CR]format\f[R], \f[CR]format\-buffer\f[R] (as \f[CR]:format\f[R] and
\f[CR]:%format\f[R]), \f[CR]fill\-paragraph\f[R] (as \f[CR]gq\f[R] on
the paragraph), \f[CR]isearch\-forward\f[R],
\f[CR]isearch\-backward\f[R], \f[CR]kill\-kosh\f[R] (as
\f[CR]Ctrl\-X Ctrl\-C\f[R]), \f[CR]undo\f[R], \f[CR]undo\-redo\f[R],
\f[CR]beginning\-of\-line\f[R], \f[CR]end\-of\-line\f[R],
\f[CR]forward\-word\f[R], \f[CR]backward\-word\f[R],
\f[CR]scroll\-down\-command\f[R], \f[CR]scroll\-up\-command\f[R],
\f[CR]beginning\-of\-history\f[R], \f[CR]end\-of\-history\f[R],
\f[CR]delete\-char\f[R], \f[CR]backward\-delete\-char\f[R],
\f[CR]kill\-word\f[R], \f[CR]backward\-kill\-word\f[R],
\f[CR]kill\-line\f[R], \f[CR]unix\-line\-discard\f[R], \f[CR]yank\f[R],
\f[CR]yank\-last\-arg\f[R], \f[CR]transpose\-chars\f[R],
\f[CR]transpose\-words\f[R], \f[CR]upcase\-word\f[R],
\f[CR]downcase\-word\f[R], \f[CR]capitalize\-word\f[R],
\f[CR]delete\-horizontal\-space\f[R], \f[CR]clear\-screen\f[R].
T}
T{
Multi\-cursor (\f[CR]Ctrl\-V\f[R])
T}@T{
\f[CR]Up\f[R]/\f[CR]Down\f[R]/\f[CR]Ctrl\-P\f[R]/\f[CR]Ctrl\-N\f[R] add
cursors vertically;
\f[CR]Left\f[R]/\f[CR]Right\f[R]/\f[CR]Home\f[R]/\f[CR]End\f[R]/\f[CR]Ctrl\-B\f[R]/\f[CR]Ctrl\-F\f[R]/\f[CR]Ctrl\-A\f[R]/\f[CR]Ctrl\-E\f[R]
move all cursors; typing and \f[CR]Backspace\f[R] edit at all cursors;
\f[CR]Ctrl\-G\f[R], \f[CR]Escape\f[R], and unrecognized keys leave
multi\-cursor mode; \f[CR]Enter\f[R], \f[CR]Ctrl\-D\f[R], and
\f[CR]Ctrl\-C\f[R] leave it and behave as in Emacs mode.
T}
T{
Completion menu
T}@T{
\f[CR]Down\f[R]/\f[CR]Ctrl\-N\f[R]/\f[CR]Up\f[R]/\f[CR]Ctrl\-P\f[R]/\f[CR]Shift\-Tab\f[R]
cycle rows; \f[CR]Tab\f[R] accepts (opening directories);
\f[CR]Right\f[R] accepts and chains completion; \f[CR]Enter\f[R] closes
menu and runs command; typing or \f[CR]Backspace\f[R] narrows or widens
the rows; \f[CR]Escape\f[R] closes the menu and keeps the edited line;
\f[CR]Ctrl\-G\f[R] and unrecognized keys close the menu and restore the
original line; any other key closes the menu, then acts on the line.
T}
T{
History search
T}@T{
In \f[CR]interactive\f[R] mode: \f[CR]Enter\f[R]/\f[CR]Tab\f[R] accept
without running; \f[CR]Escape\f[R], \f[CR]Ctrl\-G\f[R], and unrecognized
keys cancel and restore the line; other keys behave as in the completion
menu.
In \f[CR]plain\f[R] mode:
\f[CR]Down\f[R]/\f[CR]Ctrl\-N\f[R]/\f[CR]Ctrl\-R\f[R] step to an older
match;
\f[CR]Up\f[R]/\f[CR]Ctrl\-P\f[R]/\f[CR]Ctrl\-F\f[R]/\f[CR]Shift\-Tab\f[R]
step to a newer match; typing or \f[CR]Backspace\f[R] extends or
shortens the query; \f[CR]Enter\f[R]/\f[CR]Tab\f[R] accept the match
without running it; \f[CR]Escape\f[R], \f[CR]Ctrl\-G\f[R], and
unrecognized keys cancel and restore the line;
\f[CR]Ctrl\-C\f[R]/\f[CR]Ctrl\-D\f[R] cancel, restore the line, and act
on it; any other key accepts the match, then acts on the line.
T}
.TE
.SS Prompt rendering and escape sequences
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[B]Prompt lifecycle\f[R] \- Before reading interactive input, the
shell executes \f[CR]PROMPT_COMMAND\f[R] (a single command or an indexed
array of commands executed sequentially, preserving the prior
command\[aq]s \f[CR]$?\f[R] and \f[CR]$_\f[R]) and prints \f[CR]PS1\f[R]
and the right prompt (\f[CR]RPS1\f[R], or \f[CR]RPROMPT\f[R] if
\f[CR]RPS1\f[R] is unset/empty, defaulting to dim
\f[CR]\[rs]L \[rs]M\f[R] in an interactive shell started with neither
set).
The right prompt expands like \f[CR]PS1\f[R], drops blanks at either
end, and is drawn on the first input row unless no room remains or it
holds a control character other than a color sequence.
The default \f[CR]PS1\f[R] shows the Git branch with ahead/behind
counts, user, host, shortened directory (\f[CR]\[rs]P\f[R]), and status
bullet (\f[CR]\[rs].\f[R]).
After reading input and before execution, \f[CR]PS0\f[R] prints.
\f[CR]PS2\f[R] defaults to \f[CR]> \f[R] (unused by the interactive
editor, which submits full multi\-line buffers on \f[CR]Enter\f[R]),
\f[CR]PS3\f[R] prompts for \f[CR]select\f[R] (\f[CR]#? \f[R] default),
and \f[CR]PS4\f[R] prefixes \f[CR]xtrace\f[R] lines (\f[CR]+ \f[R]
default, repeating its first byte per nesting level of substitution,
\f[CR]eval\f[R], \f[CR]source\f[R], or trap).
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[B]Expansion and transient prompts\f[R] \- \f[CR]PS0\f[R],
\f[CR]PS1\f[R], \f[CR]PS2\f[R], and \f[CR]RPS1\f[R]/\f[CR]RPROMPT\f[R]
process backslash escapes first, then undergo parameter, command, and
arithmetic expansion (\f[CR]PS4\f[R] prints literally).
Setting non\-empty \f[CR]KOSH_TRANSIENT_PS1\f[R] or
\f[CR]KOSH_TRANSIENT_RPS1\f[R] replaces \f[CR]PS1\f[R] and
\f[CR]RPS1\f[R] in scrollback upon \f[CR]Enter\f[R] or
\f[CR]Ctrl\-C\f[R] (an interactive shell started without
\f[CR]KOSH_TRANSIENT_RPS1\f[R] sets it to \f[CR]\[rs][\[rs]]\f[R], which
erases the right prompt after submission).
For example, \f[CR]KOSH_TRANSIENT_PS1=\[aq]\[rs]$ \[aq]\f[R] leaves
\f[CR]$ \f[R] before each command in the scrollback, and
\f[CR]KOSH_TRANSIENT_RPS1=\[aq]\[rs]L\[aq]\f[R] keeps each duration.
The terminal window title displays \f[CR]user \[at] directory\f[R] while
idle and the active command while executing, and output of
\f[CR]PROMPT_COMMAND\f[R] or \f[CR]PS1\f[R] can replace the idle title.
.PP
