\f[CR]KOSH_ANSI_*\f[R]
T}@T{
Overwritable, unexported
T}@T{
Terminal escape sequences (\f[CR]BLACK\f[R], \f[CR]RED\f[R],
\f[CR]GREEN\f[R], \f[CR]YELLOW\f[R], \f[CR]BLUE\f[R],
\f[CR]MAGENTA\f[R], \f[CR]CYAN\f[R], \f[CR]WHITE\f[R],
\f[CR]BRIGHT_*\f[R], \f[CR]BOLD\f[R], \f[CR]DIM\f[R], \f[CR]RESET\f[R]);
empty when color is disabled.
T}
T{
\f[CR]KOSH_ANALYSIS\f[R]
T}@T{
Exported
T}@T{
Space\-separated analysis state (\f[CR]mimicry\f[R] for \f[CR]\-I\f[R],
\f[CR]warnings=N\f[R] for \f[CR]\-W\f[R], \f[CR]no\-annoying\f[R],
\f[CR]no\-diagnostics\f[R]; \f[CR]no\-annoying\f[R] is
\f[CR]optimizer.show_annoying_tier\f[R] off and
\f[CR]no\-diagnostics\f[R] is
\f[CR]optimizer.analyze_before_running\f[R] off).
Each \f[CR]set\f[R] rewrites it, and the variable is removed when empty.
A launched shell applies the inherited value, and an explicit
\f[CR]\-W\f[R] replaces the inherited level.
Command\-line options do not set it.
T}
T{
\f[CR]KOSH_GIT_BRANCH\f[R], \f[CR]KOSH_GIT_AHEAD\f[R],
\f[CR]KOSH_GIT_BEHIND\f[R]
T}@T{
Overwritable
T}@T{
Active Git branch (or short detached commit hash) and upstream
ahead/behind counts (empty when \f[CR]0\f[R] or unavailable; the search
stops at \f[CR]GIT_CEILING_DIRECTORIES\f[R]).
An assignment replaces the value.
T}
T{
\f[CR]KOSH_PS1_*\f[R]
T}@T{
Read\-only
T}@T{
Current text of each prompt escape (see Prompt rendering).
Assignments are ignored.
T}
T{
\f[CR]KOSHCONF\f[R]
T}@T{
Read\-only, unexported
T}@T{
Dynamic Base64\-encoded binary snapshot of active mood and interactive
settings (format in Binary wire format).
Assignments are discarded, and the shell never exports it by itself.
T}
