T{
Utility
T}@T{
Operational specification and flags
T}
_
T{
\f[CR]calc\f[R]
T}@T{
Evaluates arbitrary\-precision integer and finite decimal expressions
from operands, \f[CR]\-i\f[R] (\f[CR]\-\-interactive\f[R] with
\f[CR]Ctrl\-R\f[R] search of the calc history), or \f[CR]\-p\f[R]
(\f[CR]\-\-pipe\f[R], one expression per standard input line, no
prompt).
Builtin functions: \f[CR]abs\f[R], \f[CR]atan\f[R], \f[CR]ceil\f[R],
\f[CR]cmp\f[R], \f[CR]cos\f[R], \f[CR]exp\f[R], \f[CR]fact\f[R],
\f[CR]fib\f[R], \f[CR]floor\f[R], \f[CR]frac\f[R], \f[CR]gcd\f[R],
\f[CR]int\f[R], \f[CR]iseven\f[R], \f[CR]isint\f[R], \f[CR]isodd\f[R],
\f[CR]length\f[R], \f[CR]lcm\f[R], \f[CR]ln\f[R], \f[CR]max\f[R],
\f[CR]min\f[R], \f[CR]scale\f[R], \f[CR]sgn\f[R], \f[CR]sin\f[R],
\f[CR]sqrt\f[R].
T}
T{
\f[CR]evil\f[R]
T}@T{
Prints system identity, uptime, CPU, memory, swap, filesystem, process,
and network summary (\f[CR]\-a\f[R] detailed, \f[CR]\-s\f[R] select
identity fields, \f[CR]\-u\f[R] local users).
Shared flags of \f[CR]evilio\f[R], \f[CR]evilnet\f[R],
\f[CR]evilps\f[R], and \f[CR]evilss\f[R]:
\f[CR]\-l\f[R]/\f[CR]\-\-live[=N]\f[R] (\f[CR]evilss\f[R] takes only
\f[CR]\-\-live\f[R]) refreshes every \f[CR]N\f[R] seconds (default
\f[CR]0.5\f[R]) on the alternate screen until \f[CR]q\f[R] (status
\f[CR]0\f[R]) or an interrupt (status \f[CR]130\f[R]), and a tall frame
scrolls with \f[CR]j\f[R], \f[CR]k\f[R], the arrow and page keys,
\f[CR]g\f[R], \f[CR]G\f[R], and the mouse wheel.
\f[CR]evilio\f[R], \f[CR]evilnet\f[R], and \f[CR]evilps\f[R] also take
\f[CR]\-C\f[R]/\f[CR]\-\-cumulative[=M]\f[R] (change over \f[CR]M\f[R]
seconds, default \f[CR]1\f[R]; a rolling \f[CR]M\f[R]\-second window
with \f[CR]\-\-live\f[R]) and \f[CR]\-\-sort\f[R] (a metric or its
shortest unambiguous prefix).
T}
T{
\f[CR]evildisk\f[R]
T}@T{
Prints disk capacity, filesystem identity, and error/retry totals
(\f[CR]\-a\f[R] adds labels, UUIDs, error counters, and SMART telemetry;
accepts optional device/file filters).
T}
T{
\f[CR]evilfiles\f[R]
T}@T{
Lists open file descriptors filtered by \f[CR]\-p\f[R] (PID),
\f[CR]\-u\f[R] (owner), \f[CR]\-c\f[R] (command prefix), \f[CR]\-i\f[R]
(sockets), \f[CR]\-t\f[R] (terse PIDs),
\f[CR]\-w\f[R]/\f[CR]\-\-wide\f[R] (untruncated), and optional path
operands.
T}
T{
\f[CR]evilfs\f[R]
T}@T{
Prints mounted filesystems.
T}
T{
\f[CR]evilio\f[R]
T}@T{
Prints memory, swap, and cumulative disk I/O counters (\f[CR]\-a\f[R]
samples 1s CPU/paging/scheduler/PSI/disk/swap rates;
\f[CR]\-h\f[R]/\f[CR]\-\-human\-readable\f[R] binary units; per\-process
counters with \f[CR]\-\-ps\f[R] for every process,
\f[CR]\-n COUNT\f[R]/\f[CR]\-NUMBER\f[R] for that many rows,
\f[CR]\-p PID\f[R] for one process).
Supports \f[CR]\-l\f[R]/\f[CR]\-\-live[=N]\f[R],
\f[CR]\-C\f[R]/\f[CR]\-\-cumulative[=M]\f[R], and \f[CR]\-\-sort\f[R]
(\f[CR]pid\f[R], \f[CR]read\f[R], \f[CR]write\f[R],
\f[CR]read\-ops\f[R], \f[CR]write\-ops\f[R], \f[CR]busy\f[R],
\f[CR]read\-latency\f[R], \f[CR]write\-latency\f[R],
\f[CR]average\-queue\f[R], \f[CR]queue\f[R], \f[CR]errors\f[R],
\f[CR]retries\f[R]).
T}
T{
\f[CR]eviliso\f[R]
T}@T{
Inspects isolation primitives: namespaces (\f[CR]\-n\f[R]), cgroups
(\f[CR]\-c\f[R]), login sessions (\f[CR]\-s\f[R]), remote sockets
(\f[CR]\-r\f[R]), container runtimes (\f[CR]\-k\f[R],
\f[CR]\-\-container\f[R]), and Kubernetes pods
(\f[CR]\-\-kubernetes\f[R], reading \f[CR]KUBERNETES_SERVICE_HOST\f[R],
service\-account namespace, and \f[CR]kubepods\f[R] cgroups), with
\f[CR]\-a\f[R] for detailed rows.
Without a selector it prints every section.
T}
T{
\f[CR]evillogs\f[R]
T}@T{
Prints core dump settings, dump reports, and log directories, or only
one part with \f[CR]\-\-cores\f[R] or \f[CR]\-\-logs\f[R].
T}
T{
\f[CR]evilnet\f[R]
T}@T{
Reports IPv4/IPv6 interface addresses (\f[CR]\-a\f[R] adds traffic,
errors, drops, and TCP counters; \f[CR]\-f\f[R] TCP failure/loss only;
\f[CR]\-t\f[R]/\f[CR]\-\-traffic\f[R] traffic table only; supports
\f[CR]\-l\f[R]/\f[CR]\-\-live[=N]\f[R],
\f[CR]\-C\f[R]/\f[CR]\-\-cumulative[=M]\f[R], and \f[CR]\-\-sort\f[R] by
\f[CR]name\f[R], \f[CR]rx\f[R], \f[CR]tx\f[R], \f[CR]rx\-packets\f[R],
\f[CR]tx\-packets\f[R], \f[CR]rx\-errors\f[R], \f[CR]tx\-errors\f[R],
\f[CR]rx\-drops\f[R], \f[CR]tx\-drops\f[R]).
T}
T{
\f[CR]evilps\f[R]
T}@T{
Renders process hierarchy tree, limited to the PID operands when given
(\f[CR]\-p\f[R] PID column, \f[CR]\-n\f[R] numeric sort, \f[CR]\-a\f[R]
all fields, \f[CR]\-A\f[R] command lines, \f[CR]\-U\f[R] owners,
\f[CR]\-c\f[R] CPU, \f[CR]\-M\f[R] memory,
\f[CR]\-w\f[R]/\f[CR]\-\-wide\f[R] untruncated, \f[CR]\-NUMBER\f[R] row
limit, \f[CR]\-l\f[R]/\f[CR]\-\-live[=N]\f[R] with \f[CR]s\f[R] sort
cycle and \f[CR]/\f[R] search,
\f[CR]\-C\f[R]/\f[CR]\-\-cumulative[=M]\f[R], and \f[CR]\-\-sort\f[R] by
\f[CR]name\f[R], \f[CR]pid\f[R], \f[CR]cpu\f[R], \f[CR]memory\f[R]).
T}
T{
\f[CR]evilss\f[R]
T}@T{
Lists sockets filtered by \f[CR]\-l\f[R] (listening), \f[CR]\-a\f[R]
(all), \f[CR]\-t\f[R] (TCP), \f[CR]\-u\f[R] (UDP), \f[CR]\-x\f[R]
(Unix), \f[CR]\-4\f[R], \f[CR]\-6\f[R], \f[CR]\-p\f[R] (owning process),
\f[CR]\-n\f[R] (numeric addresses), \f[CR]\-H\f[R] (no header), and
\f[CR]\-\-live\f[R].
T}
T{
\f[CR]goodcore\f[R]
T}@T{
Captures live process core (\f[CR]\-p PID\f[R]) or packages an existing
core and binary (\f[CR]\-b\f[R]), bundling \f[CR]dump/core\f[R], the
executable and its shared libraries under \f[CR]root/\f[R], and
\f[CR]debug\-gdb.sh\f[R] / \f[CR]debug\-lldb.sh\f[R] wrappers into
\f[CR]goodcore\-<core>.tar.zst\f[R] (\f[CR].tar.gz\f[R] when zstd is
missing, a plain tar with \f[CR]\-\-no\-compress\f[R],
\f[CR]\-o PATH\f[R] output, \f[CR]\-q\f[R] quiet).
T}
T{
\f[CR]goodfsw\f[R]
T}@T{
Reports path changes by scanning metadata at most once per latency
period; on Linux a scan follows an \f[CR]inotify\f[R] event and a quiet
tree is rescanned every 30 periods, and elsewhere, or when a watch
fails, a scan runs every period.
A record holds the Unix scan time, numeric event mask, and path
(\f[CR]\-m\f[R], the default).
Supports \f[CR]\-h\f[R] (human timestamps and event labels),
\f[CR]\-\-timezone\f[R] (\f[CR]local\f[R] or \f[CR]utc\f[R]) and
\f[CR]\-\-precision\f[R] (\f[CR]0\f[R]..\f[CR]9\f[R] fraction digits)
for human timestamps, \f[CR]\-r\f[R] (recursive),
\f[CR]\-\-event\-flags\f[R] (append labels), \f[CR]\-x\f[R] (one
filesystem), \f[CR]\-1\f[R] (single batch), \f[CR]\-l\f[R] (latency
period, default \f[CR]1\f[R] second), and \f[CR]\-e\f[R] (exclude
substring).
T}
T{
\f[CR]goodnode\f[R]
T}@T{
Reports inode identity, allocation blocks, filesystem capabilities,
verification state, and a CRC32C checksum for each path (\f[CR]\-i\f[R]
locates an inode under \f[CR]\-r PATH\f[R]; \f[CR]\-\-verify\f[R] runs
the native filesystem verification where supported).
T}
T{
\f[CR]goodstat\f[R]
T}@T{
Prints labeled file metadata (\f[CR]\-L\f[R] dereference symlinks,
\f[CR]\-c\f[R] include CRC32C checksum, \f[CR]\-f\f[R] filesystem
capacity report).
T}
T{
\f[CR]meow\f[R]
T}@T{
Renders an animated pixel\-art cat screensaver
(\f[CR]\-f\f[R]/\f[CR]\-\-fps\f[R] \f[CR]1\f[R]..\f[CR]240\f[R], default
\f[CR]60\f[R]; \f[CR]\-s\f[R]/\f[CR]\-\-speed\f[R]
\f[CR]0.1\f[R]..\f[CR]10\f[R]; \f[CR]\-n\f[R]/\f[CR]\-\-cats\f[R]
\f[CR]1\f[R]..\f[CR]8\f[R]; \f[CR]Space\f[R] pauses,
\f[CR]+\f[R]/\f[CR]\-\f[R] adjusts speed, and any other key exits).
T}
T{
\f[CR]retry\f[R]
T}@T{
Repeats a command until it succeeds or the attempts run out, using
\f[CR]\-n\f[R] (max attempts), \f[CR]\-d\f[R] (initial delay),
\f[CR]\-b\f[R] (backoff multiplier), \f[CR]\-m\f[R] (max delay), and
\f[CR]\-q\f[R] (quiet).
T}
T{
\f[CR]slurp\f[R], \f[CR]vi\f[R], \f[CR]emacs\f[R]
T}@T{
Edits text files as the \f[CR]slurp\f[R] builtin does, with the same
options and \f[CR]+LINE\f[R] operand (\f[CR]vi\f[R] implies
\f[CR]\-V\f[R]; \f[CR]emacs\f[R] implies \f[CR]\-e\f[R]).
T}
.TE
.SS Standard POSIX and Unix utilities
.PP
.TS
tab(@);
l l.
T{
Utility
T}@T{
Supported flags and behavioral specification
T}
_
T{
\f[CR]basename\f[R]
T}@T{
Prints the final path component, minus an optional suffix
(\f[CR]\-a\f[R]/\f[CR]\-\-multiple\f[R] treat every operand as a path,
\f[CR]\-s\f[R]/\f[CR]\-\-suffix\f[R] remove a suffix from each and imply
\f[CR]\-a\f[R], \f[CR]\-z\f[R]/\f[CR]\-\-zero\f[R] end entries with
NUL).
T}
T{
\f[CR]bc\f[R]
T}@T{
Evaluates expressions, assignments, functions, arrays, control flow,
input and output bases, and scale, from the file operands and then
standard input (\f[CR]\-l\f[R] adds the functions \f[CR]s\f[R] sine,
\f[CR]c\f[R] cosine, \f[CR]a\f[R] arctangent, \f[CR]l\f[R] natural
logarithm, \f[CR]e\f[R] exponential and sets scale to \f[CR]20\f[R];
\f[CR]\-q\f[R] suppress the banner).
Division by zero stops the input with status \f[CR]1\f[R].
T}
T{
\f[CR]cal\f[R]
T}@T{
Prints a Gregorian month or year with weeks starting on Sunday
(\f[CR]\-a\f[R]/\f[CR]\-\-today\f[R] start weeks on Monday and print the
date in words below).
T}
T{
\f[CR]cat\f[R]
T}@T{
Concatenates files or standard input (\f[CR]\-n\f[R] number lines across
files, \f[CR]\-b\f[R] number nonempty lines, \f[CR]\-s\f[R] squeeze
empty runs, \f[CR]\-v\f[R] show control bytes in \f[CR]\[ha]\f[R]
notation and high bytes with \f[CR]M\-\f[R], \f[CR]\-E\f[R] mark line
ends with \f[CR]$\f[R] and a CR before a newline as \f[CR]\[ha]M\f[R],
\f[CR]\-T\f[R] show tabs as \f[CR]\[ha]I\f[R],
\f[CR]\-e\f[R]/\f[CR]\-t\f[R]/\f[CR]\-A\f[R] act as
\f[CR]\-vE\f[R]/\f[CR]\-vT\f[R]/\f[CR]\-vET\f[R], \f[CR]\-u\f[R]
accepted, \f[CR]\-\-syntax\-highlighting\f[R] colors shell source on a
terminal).
T}
T{
\f[CR]chgrp\f[R], \f[CR]chown\f[R]
T}@T{
Changes the group (\f[CR]chgrp\f[R]), or the owner and optional group
(\f[CR]chown\f[R]), of each file (\f[CR]\-R\f[R] recurse,
\f[CR]\-H\f[R]/\f[CR]\-L\f[R]/\f[CR]\-P\f[R] select which links are
followed, \f[CR]\-h\f[R] change a link itself,
\f[CR]\-x\f[R]/\f[CR]\-\-one\-file\-system\f[R] keep recursion on one
file system).
T}
T{
\f[CR]chmod\f[R]
T}@T{
Applies symbolic or octal modes.
\f[CR]\-R\f[R]/\f[CR]\-\-recursive\f[R] recurses without following
links, and \f[CR]\-\-one\-file\-system\f[R] skips other file systems.
T}
T{
\f[CR]cksum\f[R]
T}@T{
Prints POSIX CRC checksum, byte count, and filename.
T}
T{
\f[CR]cmp\f[R]
T}@T{
Compares two files byte by byte (\f[CR]0\f[R] equal, \f[CR]1\f[R]
different with the first differing byte and line printed, \f[CR]2\f[R]
unreadable file; \f[CR]\-l\f[R]/\f[CR]\-\-verbose\f[R] list every
differing byte with both values in octal,
\f[CR]\-s\f[R]/\f[CR]\-\-silent\f[R] print nothing).
A file of \f[CR]\-\f[R] is standard input.
T}
T{
\f[CR]comm\f[R]
T}@T{
Merges two sorted files into columns of lines only in the first, only in
the second, and in both (\f[CR]\-1\f[R]/\f[CR]\-2\f[R]/\f[CR]\-3\f[R]
suppress them, \f[CR]\-\-check\-order\f[R] stop at the first line out of
order, \f[CR]\-\-nocheck\-order\f[R] skip the check, the later one wins,
\f[CR]\-\-output\-delimiter\f[R] column separator with empty for NUL,
\f[CR]\-\-total\f[R] append column counts, \f[CR]\-z\f[R] NUL line
ends).
A line out of order after an unpaired line is reported once per file
with status \f[CR]1\f[R].
T}
T{
\f[CR]cp\f[R]
T}@T{
Copies files and trees (\f[CR]\-r\f[R]/\f[CR]\-R\f[R] recurse,
\f[CR]\-f\f[R], \f[CR]\-i\f[R], \f[CR]\-p\f[R], \f[CR]\-v\f[R],
\f[CR]\-L\f[R] follow every link, \f[CR]\-H\f[R] follow links on the
command line only, \f[CR]\-P\f[R] follow none,
\f[CR]\-x\f[R]/\f[CR]\-\-one\-file\-system\f[R] copy a directory on
another file system as an empty directory).
A recursive copy keeps links as links.
A link leading back into a directory being copied is reported as cyclic
and skipped with status \f[CR]1\f[R].
T}
T{
\f[CR]csplit\f[R]
T}@T{
Splits a file into pieces \f[CR]xx00\f[R], \f[CR]xx01\f[R], and so on at
each pattern, which is a line number or a \f[CR]/regex/\f[R], and prints
the byte count of each piece (\f[CR]\-f\f[R]/\f[CR]\-\-prefix\f[R]
replace \f[CR]xx\f[R], \f[CR]\-n\f[R]/\f[CR]\-\-digits\f[R] number of
digits, \f[CR]\-s\f[R]/\f[CR]\-\-silent\f[R] suppress the counts,
\f[CR]\-k\f[R]/\f[CR]\-\-keep\-files\f[R] keep the pieces after an
error).
Returns \f[CR]1\f[R] for a line number past the input or a regex that
does not match.
T}
T{
\f[CR]cut\f[R]
T}@T{
Selects bytes (\f[CR]\-b\f[R]), characters (\f[CR]\-c\f[R]), or fields
(\f[CR]\-f\f[R]) (\f[CR]\-d\f[R] delimiter, \f[CR]\-s\f[R] skip lines
without one, \f[CR]\-\-complement\f[R] invert the selection,
\f[CR]\-\-output\-delimiter=STR\f[R] join selections with
\f[CR]STR\f[R], \f[CR]\-z\f[R]/\f[CR]\-\-zero\-terminated\f[R] NUL line
ends, \f[CR]\-n\f[R] with \f[CR]\-b\f[R] leave out a multibyte character
that the byte range splits).
Returns \f[CR]1\f[R] for an invalid list or a delimiter longer than one
byte.
T}
T{
\f[CR]date\f[R]
T}@T{
Prints the date and time, or formats them with a \f[CR]+format\f[R]
operand of strftime conversions (\f[CR]\-u\f[R]/\f[CR]\-\-utc\f[R] use
UTC).
Refuses an operand that would set the clock.
T}
T{
\f[CR]df\f[R]
T}@T{
Reports mounted file systems, or those of the operands, in a
right\-aligned table (\f[CR]\-k\f[R] \f[CR]1024\f[R]\-byte blocks,
\f[CR]\-P\f[R] POSIX header,
\f[CR]\-h\f[R]/\f[CR]\-\-human\-readable\f[R] powers of \f[CR]1024\f[R],
\f[CR]\-H\f[R]/\f[CR]\-\-si\f[R] powers of \f[CR]1000\f[R]).
Unreadable file systems are reported before the table.
T}
T{
\f[CR]diff\f[R]
T}@T{
Compares two files line by line (\f[CR]\-u\f[R] unified output,
\f[CR]\-w\f[R] ignore whitespace, \f[CR]\-a\f[R] force text, up to two
\f[CR]\-L\f[R] set the unified labels, \f[CR]\-\-color[=WHEN]\f[R] with
\f[CR]auto\f[R] default, \f[CR]always\f[R], \f[CR]never\f[R];
\f[CR]0\f[R] equal, \f[CR]1\f[R] different, \f[CR]2\f[R] error).
T}
T{
\f[CR]dirname\f[R]
T}@T{
Prints the directory part of each path.
\f[CR]\-z\f[R]/\f[CR]\-\-zero\f[R] ends entries with NUL.
T}
T{
\f[CR]du\f[R]
T}@T{
Prints every file and directory below each path, or the current
directory, in descending size order without following links
(\f[CR]\-s\f[R] totals only, \f[CR]\-h\f[R] human\-readable sizes,
\f[CR]\-x\f[R]/\f[CR]\-\-one\-file\-system\f[R] skip other file systems,
\f[CR]\-\-tree\f[R] print a tree,
\f[CR]\-T\f[R]/\f[CR]\-\-top\-largest\f[R] print a tree of the largest
entries and their ancestors).
Permission errors are warnings and other read failures are errors;
either makes the status \f[CR]1\f[R].
T}
T{
\f[CR]env\f[R]
T}@T{
Runs a command with temporary assignments, or prints the environment
(\f[CR]\-i\f[R] start empty, \f[CR]\-u VAR\f[R] remove a variable,
repeatable).
Finds the command through its \f[CR]PATH\f[R], or
\f[CR]/usr/bin:/bin\f[R] without one.
T}
T{
\f[CR]expand\f[R], \f[CR]unexpand\f[R]
T}@T{
Converts tabs to spaces (\f[CR]expand\f[R]) or blanks to tabs
(\f[CR]unexpand\f[R]) (\f[CR]\-t\f[R] ascending tab stops separated by
commas or blanks, or one interval; a last value \f[CR]/N\f[R] adds a
stop at each multiple of \f[CR]N\f[R], and \f[CR]+N\f[R] one every
\f[CR]N\f[R] columns, after the last explicit stop; default every eight
columns; \f[CR]unexpand \-a\f[R] also converts blanks after the first
nonblank, and \f[CR]\-t\f[R] implies it).
T}
T{
\f[CR]expr\f[R]
T}@T{
Evaluates an expression whose operators and operands are separate
arguments and prints the result (\f[CR]|\f[R], \f[CR]&\f[R],
\f[CR]=\f[R], \f[CR]!=\f[R], \f[CR]<\f[R], \f[CR]<=\f[R], \f[CR]>\f[R],
\f[CR]>=\f[R], \f[CR]+\f[R], \f[CR]\-\f[R], \f[CR]*\f[R], \f[CR]/\f[R],
\f[CR]%\f[R], and \f[CR]:\f[R], which matches a basic regular expression
anchored at the start and prints the first group or the match length).
Returns \f[CR]0\f[R] for a result that is neither \f[CR]0\f[R] nor empty
and \f[CR]1\f[R] otherwise.
An invalid expression, integer overflow, and division by zero are errors
that return \f[CR]2\f[R] in \f[CR]sh\f[R] and \f[CR]1\f[R] in Bash
moods, and are fatal in \f[CR]kosh\f[R].
T}
T{
\f[CR]file\f[R]
T}@T{
Classifies file kinds and contents
(\f[CR]\-h\f[R]/\f[CR]\-\-no\-dereference\f[R] classify a link,
\f[CR]\-L\f[R]/\f[CR]\-\-dereference\f[R] its target,
\f[CR]\-i\f[R]/\f[CR]\-\-regular\-only\f[R] skip content tests,
\f[CR]\-m\f[R]/\f[CR]\-\-magic\-file\f[R] add a magic database,
\f[CR]\-M\f[R]/\f[CR]\-\-magic\-only\f[R] use only the given ones,
\f[CR]\-d\f[R]/\f[CR]\-\-default\-tests\f[R] select the default tests).
The kinds include text, data, directory, the special files, ELF
executable, common image formats, script text executable, and symbolic
link to a target.
Returns \f[CR]1\f[R] for a file that cannot be opened.
T}
T{
\f[CR]find\f[R]
T}@T{
Walks sorted trees (\f[CR]\-name\f[R], \f[CR]\-iname\f[R],
\f[CR]\-type\f[R], \f[CR]\-maxdepth\f[R], \f[CR]\-mindepth\f[R],
\f[CR]\-print\f[R], \f[CR]\-print0\f[R],
\f[CR]\-xdev\f[R]/\f[CR]\-mount\f[R] stay on one file system,
\f[CR]\-exec COMMAND ... ;\f[R] run once per path with \f[CR]{}\f[R]
replaced, \f[CR]\-exec COMMAND {} +\f[R] run on batches of paths).
T}
T{
\f[CR]flock\f[R]
T}@T{
Runs a command while holding a lock on a file or directory, which the
command inherits as a descriptor (\f[CR]\-n\f[R]/\f[CR]\-\-nonblock\f[R]
fail with status \f[CR]1\f[R] instead of waiting,
\f[CR]\-\-transaction\-held\-lock\f[R] keep the lock after the launching
process exits).
T}
T{
\f[CR]fold\f[R]
T}@T{
Wraps the lines of each file or standard input at \f[CR]80\f[R] columns
(\f[CR]\-w\f[R]/\f[CR]\-\-width\f[R] set the width,
\f[CR]\-s\f[R]/\f[CR]\-\-spaces\f[R] break after the last blank when one
fits, \f[CR]\-b\f[R]/\f[CR]\-\-bytes\f[R] count bytes).
A tab advances to the next multiple of eight.
T}
T{
\f[CR]fuser\f[R]
T}@T{
Prints the PIDs that use each file, with \f[CR]\-c\f[R], \f[CR]\-f\f[R],
and \f[CR]\-u\f[R].
T}
T{
\f[CR]getconf\f[R]
T}@T{
Prints a system or string variable, or a path variable for a path
(\f[CR]\-a\f[R]/\f[CR]\-\-all\f[R] print every variable,
\f[CR]\-v\f[R]/\f[CR]\-\-specification\f[R] select a POSIX environment).
Prints \f[CR]undefined\f[R] for an unsupported variable.
T}
T{
\f[CR]grep\f[R], \f[CR]egrep\f[R], \f[CR]fgrep\f[R]
T}@T{
Prints lines matching basic regular expressions, extended ones with
\f[CR]\-E\f[R] (\f[CR]egrep\f[R]), or fixed strings with \f[CR]\-F\f[R]
(\f[CR]fgrep\f[R]); \f[CR]\-E\f[R] and \f[CR]\-F\f[R] together return
\f[CR]2\f[R].
Patterns come from the first operand, \f[CR]\-e\f[R] (add a pattern), or
\f[CR]\-f\f[R] (lines of a file); with \f[CR]\-e\f[R] or \f[CR]\-f\f[R]
every operand is a file, and a newline separates patterns.
Options: \f[CR]\-i\f[R] ignore case, \f[CR]\-v\f[R] invert,
\f[CR]\-x\f[R] match whole lines, \f[CR]\-n\f[R] number lines,
\f[CR]\-h\f[R] omit file prefixes, \f[CR]\-r\f[R] recurse
(\f[CR]\-\-one\-file\-system\f[R] stays on one file system),
\f[CR]\-c\f[R] count, \f[CR]\-l\f[R] list matching files (overrides
\f[CR]\-c\f[R]), \f[CR]\-q\f[R] exit \f[CR]0\f[R] at the first match,
\f[CR]\-s\f[R] hide unreadable\-file messages,
\f[CR]\-a\f[R]/\f[CR]\-\-text\f[R] treat a file with a NUL byte as text,
\f[CR]\-\-color[=WHEN]\f[R] (\f[CR]auto\f[R] default, \f[CR]always\f[R],
\f[CR]never\f[R]).
Returns \f[CR]0\f[R] when a line is selected, \f[CR]1\f[R] when none is,
and \f[CR]2\f[R] on error.
In a file with a NUL byte and without \f[CR]\-a\f[R], matches before the
line of the first NUL print, the next match shows a single warning, and
later matches print nothing.
In a UTF\-8 locale a dot and a bracket expression match one character,
and one byte otherwise.
See the \f[CR]GREP_COLORS\f[R] bullet below the table.
T}
T{
\f[CR]head\f[R], \f[CR]tail\f[R]
T}@T{
Prints the first (\f[CR]head\f[R]) or last (\f[CR]tail\f[R]) ten lines
(\f[CR]\-n\f[R] line count, \f[CR]\-c\f[R] byte count; both accept a
suffix \f[CR]b\f[R] for 512,
\f[CR]k\f[R]/\f[CR]K\f[R]/\f[CR]m\f[R]/\f[CR]M\f[R]/\f[CR]G\f[R]/\f[CR]T\f[R]/\f[CR]P\f[R]/\f[CR]E\f[R]/\f[CR]Z\f[R]/\f[CR]Y\f[R]/\f[CR]R\f[R]/\f[CR]Q\f[R]
for powers of 1024, and those letters followed by \f[CR]B\f[R] for
powers of 1000 or by \f[CR]iB\f[R], as in \f[CR]1kB\f[R] and
\f[CR]1KiB\f[R]; a first argument such as \f[CR]\-5\f[R] means
\f[CR]\-n 5\f[R]).
For \f[CR]head\f[R], a leading dash prints all but the last N; for
\f[CR]tail\f[R], a leading plus starts at line or byte N. Headers appear
for several files
(\f[CR]\-q\f[R]/\f[CR]\-\-quiet\f[R]/\f[CR]\-\-silent\f[R] suppress
them, \f[CR]\-v\f[R]/\f[CR]\-\-verbose\f[R] forces them, the last wins);
\f[CR]\-z\f[R]/\f[CR]\-\-zero\-terminated\f[R] uses NUL line ends.
\f[CR]tail \-f\f[R] keeps printing what is appended to each regular
file; \f[CR]\-F\f[R] follows by name, reopens a replaced, removed, or
new file, and implies \f[CR]\-\-retry\f[R];
\f[CR]\-\-follow=descriptor|name\f[R] selects the mode;
\f[CR]\-s\f[R]/\f[CR]\-\-sleep\-interval\f[R] sets the longest wait
between checks (\f[CR]1\f[R] second); \f[CR]\-\-pid=PID\f[R] ends
following after that process exits.
An interrupted follow exits with status \f[CR]130\f[R].
T}
T{
\f[CR]id\f[R]
T}@T{
Prints the user and group identities of the current process or of a user
(\f[CR]\-u\f[R]/\f[CR]\-\-user\f[R] only the user,
\f[CR]\-g\f[R]/\f[CR]\-\-group\f[R] only the group,
\f[CR]\-G\f[R]/\f[CR]\-\-groups\f[R] every group,
\f[CR]\-n\f[R]/\f[CR]\-\-name\f[R] print names,
\f[CR]\-r\f[R]/\f[CR]\-\-real\f[R] use the real identities).
Returns \f[CR]1\f[R] for an unknown user.
T}
T{
\f[CR]killall\f[R], \f[CR]pkill\f[R]
T}@T{
Signals processes by exact name (\f[CR]killall\f[R]) or by a pattern
contained in the short command (\f[CR]pkill\f[R]) (signal from
\f[CR]killall \-s\f[R]/\f[CR]\-\-signal\f[R] or
\f[CR]pkill \-\-signal\f[R]/\f[CR]\-SIGNAL\f[R],
\f[CR]\-l\f[R]/\f[CR]\-\-list\f[R] list signals,
\f[CR]pkill \-s\f[R]/\f[CR]\-\-session\f[R] select comma\-separated
session IDs with \f[CR]0\f[R] for its own and an optional pattern,
\f[CR]pkill \-\-inverse\f[R] signal what the pattern and sessions do not
select).
Windows has no sessions: \f[CR]0\f[R] is rejected and nothing matches
another ID.
\f[CR]killall\f[R] never signals process 0, the shell, or the utility
itself.
T}
T{
\f[CR]less\f[R]
T}@T{
Shows files or standard input full screen on the alternate screen with
keys from the terminal (\f[CR]\-N\f[R]/\f[CR]\-\-LINE\-NUMBERS\f[R]
number lines, \f[CR]\-S\f[R]/\f[CR]\-\-chop\-long\-lines\f[R] cut long
lines instead of wrapping, \f[CR]\-i\f[R]/\f[CR]\-\-ignore\-case\f[R]
ignore case in searches).
\f[CR]/PATTERN\f[R] and \f[CR]?PATTERN\f[R] search forward and backward
with an extended regular expression, \f[CR]n\f[R]/\f[CR]N\f[R] repeat
the search, and \f[CR]q\f[R]/\f[CR]Q\f[R] quit; an interrupt quits with
status \f[CR]130\f[R].
Input loads as needed and is kept in memory up to \f[CR]128 MiB\f[R],
counting the line records; input beyond that is not shown, and the
status row adds \f[CR](truncated)\f[R].
Several files follow headers of colons.
When output is not a terminal, the input is copied unchanged.
See the \f[CR]less\f[R] keys bullet below the table.
T}
T{
\f[CR]link\f[R], \f[CR]ln\f[R] 
T}@T{
Creates hard links (\f[CR]link file1 file2\f[R] and \f[CR]ln\f[R]; an
existing \f[CR]file2\f[R] returns \f[CR]1\f[R] for \f[CR]link\f[R]) or,
with \f[CR]ln \-s\f[R], symbolic links (\f[CR]ln \-f\f[R] remove an
existing destination, \f[CR]\-L\f[R] follow a link source,
\f[CR]\-P\f[R] link the link itself).
T}
T{
\f[CR]locale\f[R]
T}@T{
Prints \f[CR]LANG\f[R] and the \f[CR]LC_\f[R] variables as the
environment sets them (\f[CR]\-a\f[R]/\f[CR]\-\-all\-locales\f[R] list
the available locales, \f[CR]\-m\f[R]/\f[CR]\-\-charmaps\f[R] the
character maps).
A keyword operand such as \f[CR]charmap\f[R] prints its value
(\f[CR]\-k\f[R]/\f[CR]\-\-keyword\-name\f[R] add the keyword,
\f[CR]\-c\f[R]/\f[CR]\-\-category\-name\f[R] add its category).
Returns \f[CR]1\f[R] for an unknown keyword.
T}
T{
\f[CR]logger\f[R]
T}@T{
Sends a message, the operands or each line of
\f[CR]\-f\f[R]/\f[CR]\-\-file\f[R], to the system log
(\f[CR]\-t\f[R]/\f[CR]\-\-tag\f[R] tag,
\f[CR]\-p\f[R]/\f[CR]\-\-priority\f[R] facility and severity as in
\f[CR]user.notice\f[R], \f[CR]\-i\f[R]/\f[CR]\-\-id\f[R] add the process
ID, \f[CR]\-s\f[R]/\f[CR]\-\-stderr\f[R] also write the message to
standard error).
Returns \f[CR]1\f[R] for an invalid priority.
T}
T{
\f[CR]logname\f[R], \f[CR]whoami\f[R], \f[CR]who\f[R]  
T}@T{
Prints the login user (\f[CR]logname\f[R]; can differ from the effective
user), the effective user (\f[CR]whoami\f[R]), or the logged\-in users
with their terminals and login times (\f[CR]who\f[R]:
\f[CR]\-a\f[R]/\f[CR]\-b\f[R]/\f[CR]\-d\f[R]/\f[CR]\-l\f[R]/\f[CR]\-p\f[R]/\f[CR]\-r\f[R]/\f[CR]\-t\f[R]/\f[CR]\-T\f[R]
select records and fields as POSIX describes, \f[CR]\-H\f[R] headings,
\f[CR]\-m\f[R] and \f[CR]am i\f[R] the terminal of standard input,
\f[CR]\-q\f[R] users and their count, \f[CR]\-s\f[R] short form,
\f[CR]\-u\f[R] idle times).
T}
T{
\f[CR]ls\f[R]
T}@T{
Lists sorted entries (\f[CR]\-a\f[R], \f[CR]\-A\f[R], \f[CR]\-1\f[R],
\f[CR]\-l\f[R], \f[CR]\-h\f[R], \f[CR]\-F\f[R] append type indicators,
\f[CR]\-p\f[R] append a slash to directories, \f[CR]\-d\f[R] list
directories themselves, \f[CR]\-n\f[R] show numeric IDs,
\f[CR]\-g\f[R]/\f[CR]\-o\f[R] omit the owner/group, \f[CR]\-t\f[R] sort
by time, \f[CR]\-S\f[R] by size, \f[CR]\-r\f[R] reverse, \f[CR]\-R\f[R]
recurse, \f[CR]\-\-tree\f[R] print a tree, \f[CR]\-L\f[R] limit depth,
\f[CR]\-\-one\-file\-system\f[R] keep recursion and tree on one file
system, \f[CR]\-k\f[R] accepted).
Without a terminal, prints one entry per line, and \f[CR]\-l\f[R] prints
a symbolic link without its target.
T}
T{
\f[CR]make\f[R]
T}@T{
Runs make rules (\f[CR]\-f\f[R]/\f[CR]\-\-file\f[R],
\f[CR]\-C\f[R]/\f[CR]\-\-directory\f[R], \f[CR]\-B\f[R] always rebuild,
\f[CR]\-k\f[R] keep going, POSIX modes \f[CR]\-e\f[R], \f[CR]\-i\f[R],
\f[CR]\-S\f[R], \f[CR]\-n\f[R], \f[CR]\-p\f[R], \f[CR]\-q\f[R],
\f[CR]\-r\f[R], \f[CR]\-s\f[R], \f[CR]\-t\f[R], and \f[CR]\-j\f[R] with
an optional job count passed through \f[CR]MAKEFLAGS\f[R]).
Without \f[CR]\-f\f[R], reads \f[CR]Makefile\f[R] or
\f[CR]makefile\f[R]; \f[CR]\-f \-\f[R] reads standard input.
Operands of the form \f[CR]NAME=VALUE\f[R] set variables, and the
environment variables are also available.
The \f[CR]wildcard\f[R] function and a prerequisite holding
\f[CR]*\f[R], \f[CR]?\f[R], or \f[CR][\f[R] use shell pathname
expansion, and an unmatched prerequisite pattern stays as written.
Recipes are printed before they run and use the \f[CR]SHELL\f[R] of the
makefile, and \f[CR]MAKE\f[R] expands to \f[CR]koshkit make\f[R].
A target without a rule returns \f[CR]2\f[R], and \f[CR]\-q\f[R] returns
\f[CR]1\f[R] when a target is out of date.
See the \f[CR]make\f[R] bullet below the table.
T}
T{
\f[CR]man\f[R]
T}@T{
Prints the source of the manual page of each operand, from the section
operand or the first section that has one, searching the directories of
\f[CR]MANPATH\f[R] (default \f[CR]/usr/share/man\f[R] and
\f[CR]/usr/local/share/man\f[R]) (\f[CR]\-k\f[R]/\f[CR]\-\-keyword\f[R]
list the pages whose first lines contain the keyword).
Returns \f[CR]1\f[R] for a missing page.
T}
T{
\f[CR]mkdir\f[R], \f[CR]rmdir\f[R] 
T}@T{
Creates directories (\f[CR]mkdir\f[R]; \f[CR]\-p\f[R] create parents,
\f[CR]\-m\f[R] octal mode or symbolic mode applied to \f[CR]777\f[R]);
removes empty directories (\f[CR]rmdir\f[R]; \f[CR]\-p\f[R] also removes
their empty parents).
T}
T{
\f[CR]mkfifo\f[R], \f[CR]mknod\f[R] 
T}@T{
Creates each FIFO with the mode of \f[CR]\-m\f[R]/\f[CR]\-\-mode\f[R],
or \f[CR]0666\f[R] less the creation mask (\f[CR]mkfifo\f[R]); creates
FIFOs and character or block special files from POSIX type operands or
\f[CR]\-\-type\f[R], \f[CR]\-\-fifo\f[R], \f[CR]\-\-character\f[R],
\f[CR]\-\-block\f[R] (\f[CR]mknod\f[R]; device nodes take
\f[CR]\-\-major\f[R] and \f[CR]\-\-minor\f[R], \f[CR]\-m\f[R] sets the
mode).
T}
T{
\f[CR]more\f[R]
T}@T{
Shows files or standard input a screen at a time with a
\f[CR]\-\-More\-\-\f[R] prompt and keys from the terminal
(\f[CR]\-n\f[R]/\f[CR]\-\-lines\f[R] lines per screen,
\f[CR]\-c\f[R]/\f[CR]\-\-clear\f[R] clear before each page,
\f[CR]\-e\f[R]/\f[CR]\-\-exit\f[R] exit after the last line,
\f[CR]\-p\f[R]/\f[CR]\-\-command\f[R] start at the first line that
matches a pattern, \f[CR]\-t\f[R]/\f[CR]\-\-tag\f[R] start at a tag of
the tags file, \f[CR]\-s\f[R]/\f[CR]\-\-squeeze\f[R] collapse repeated
blank lines, \f[CR]\-i\f[R]/\f[CR]\-\-ignore\-case\f[R] ignore case in
searches, \f[CR]\-u\f[R] accepted).
Searches work as in \f[CR]less\f[R].
Each of several files follows a header of colons, also when output is
not a terminal.
When output is not a terminal, the input is copied, changed only by
\f[CR]\-p\f[R], \f[CR]\-t\f[R], and \f[CR]\-s\f[R].
A pattern of \f[CR]\-p\f[R] may begin with a slash.
\f[CR]\-t\f[R] reads \f[CR]./tags\f[R], whose lines hold a tag, a file,
and a line separated by tabs, and takes no file operand.
\f[CR]\-p\f[R] and \f[CR]\-t\f[R] cannot be combined, and
\f[CR]more\f[R] needs a file when standard input is a terminal.
Input is kept in memory up to \f[CR]128 MiB\f[R], counting the line
records; input beyond that is not shown, and the status row adds
\f[CR](truncated)\f[R].
See the \f[CR]more\f[R] keys bullet below the table.
T}
T{
\f[CR]mv\f[R]
T}@T{
Renames or moves paths with \f[CR]\-f\f[R], \f[CR]\-i\f[R], and
\f[CR]\-v\f[R].
T}
T{
\f[CR]nice\f[R], \f[CR]renice\f[R] 
T}@T{
Runs a utility with its scheduling priority lowered by \f[CR]10\f[R], or
by the increment of \f[CR]\-n\f[R]/\f[CR]\-\-increment\f[R]
(\f[CR]nice\f[R]; a utility that is not found returns \f[CR]127\f[R]);
adds the increment of the required
\f[CR]\-n\f[R]/\f[CR]\-\-increment\f[R] to the priority of each process
(\f[CR]renice\f[R]; \f[CR]\-p\f[R]/\f[CR]\-\-pid\f[R] process IDs, the
default, \f[CR]\-g\f[R]/\f[CR]\-\-pgrp\f[R] process groups,
\f[CR]\-u\f[R]/\f[CR]\-\-user\f[R] all processes of each user).
T}
T{
\f[CR]nl\f[R]
T}@T{
Numbers lines within logical pages.
A line of only the section delimiter repeated three, two, or one times
starts a header, body, or footer and prints empty.
Options: \f[CR]\-d\f[R] delimiter (default \f[CR]\[rs]:\f[R]; a single
character gets a colon added; empty disables sections),
\f[CR]\-h\f[R]/\f[CR]\-b\f[R]/\f[CR]\-f\f[R] header/body/footer styles
(default \f[CR]n\f[R], \f[CR]t\f[R], \f[CR]n\f[R]; \f[CR]a\f[R] every
line, \f[CR]t\f[R] nonempty lines, \f[CR]n\f[R] none, \f[CR]pBRE\f[R]
lines matching the regular expression), \f[CR]\-v\f[R] starting number
(each section restarts at it unless \f[CR]\-p\f[R] is given),
\f[CR]\-i\f[R] increment (both may be negative), \f[CR]\-l\f[R] number
every Nth empty line of a run under style \f[CR]a\f[R], \f[CR]\-w\f[R]
width (at most \f[CR]65536\f[R]), \f[CR]\-n\f[R] format (\f[CR]ln\f[R],
\f[CR]rn\f[R], \f[CR]rz\f[R]), \f[CR]\-s\f[R] separator.
An overflowing line number stops with status \f[CR]1\f[R].
T}
T{
\f[CR]nohup\f[R]
T}@T{
Runs a utility that ignores \f[CR]SIGHUP\f[R].
When standard output is a terminal, appends the output to
\f[CR]nohup.out\f[R] in the current directory, or in \f[CR]HOME\f[R]
when that fails, created with mode \f[CR]0600\f[R].
Returns \f[CR]127\f[R] for a utility that is not found and
\f[CR]126\f[R] for one that cannot run.
T}
T{
\f[CR]nproc\f[R]
T}@T{
Prints the available processor count; \f[CR]\-\-all\f[R] and
\f[CR]\-\-ignore=COUNT\f[R] are supported.
T}
T{
\f[CR]od\f[R]
T}@T{
Dumps bytes in the formats of \f[CR]\-t\f[R] (types \f[CR]c\f[R],
\f[CR]o\f[R], \f[CR]u\f[R], \f[CR]d\f[R], \f[CR]x\f[R] with an optional
size; several types print one row each;
\f[CR]\-b\f[R]/\f[CR]\-c\f[R]/\f[CR]\-d\f[R]/\f[CR]\-o\f[R]/\f[CR]\-s\f[R]/\f[CR]\-x\f[R]
select
\f[CR]o1\f[R]/\f[CR]c\f[R]/\f[CR]u2\f[R]/\f[CR]o2\f[R]/\f[CR]d2\f[R]/\f[CR]x2\f[R];
\f[CR]\-A\f[R] address radix \f[CR]d\f[R], \f[CR]o\f[R], \f[CR]x\f[R],
or \f[CR]n\f[R] for none; \f[CR]\-j\f[R] skip bytes; \f[CR]\-N\f[R]
limit bytes read; \f[CR]\-v\f[R] print repeated lines otherwise shown as
\f[CR]*\f[R]).
A line holds \f[CR]16\f[R] bytes, or
\f[CR]\-w[N]\f[R]/\f[CR]\-\-width[=N]\f[R] bytes, up to
\f[CR]65536\f[R], or \f[CR]32\f[R] without \f[CR]N\f[R]; a width that is
not a multiple of the largest unit is replaced by that unit with a
warning.
T}
T{
\f[CR]paste\f[R]
T}@T{
Joins corresponding lines with tabs (\f[CR]\-d\f[R] delimiters used in
turn, \f[CR]\-s\f[R] join each file into one line,
\f[CR]\-z\f[R]/\f[CR]\-\-zero\-terminated\f[R] NUL line ends).
T}
T{
\f[CR]pathchk\f[R]
T}@T{
Checks paths against the file system limits (\f[CR]\-p\f[R] use the
POSIX portable limits and characters, \f[CR]\-P\f[R] reject an empty
path and a component starting with a hyphen,
\f[CR]\-W\f[R]/\f[CR]\-\-windows\f[R] reject what Windows cannot hold,
which Windows builds always do).
T}
T{
\f[CR]pr\f[R]
T}@T{
Paginates each file or standard input into \f[CR]66\f[R]\-line pages
with a header of the date, the file, and the page number
(\f[CR]+FIRST[:LAST]\f[R] select pages, \f[CR]\-COLUMNS\f[R] print that
many columns, \f[CR]\-a\f[R]/\f[CR]\-\-across\f[R] fill them across,
\f[CR]\-m\f[R]/\f[CR]\-\-merge\f[R] print the files side by side,
\f[CR]\-t\f[R]/\f[CR]\-\-omit\-header\f[R] omit headers,
\f[CR]\-d\f[R]/\f[CR]\-\-double\-space\f[R],
\f[CR]\-n\f[R]/\f[CR]\-\-number\-lines\f[R],
\f[CR]\-o\f[R]/\f[CR]\-\-indent\f[R],
\f[CR]\-h\f[R]/\f[CR]\-\-header\f[R] header text,
\f[CR]\-D\f[R]/\f[CR]\-\-date\-format\f[R],
\f[CR]\-l\f[R]/\f[CR]\-\-length\f[R] page length,
\f[CR]\-w\f[R]/\f[CR]\-\-width\f[R] page width,
\f[CR]\-s\f[R]/\f[CR]\-\-separator\f[R] column separator,
\f[CR]\-F\f[R]/\f[CR]\-f\f[R] separate pages with form feeds,
\f[CR]\-r\f[R]/\f[CR]\-\-no\-file\-warnings\f[R] suppress file
warnings).
T}
T{
\f[CR]printenv\f[R]
T}@T{
Prints the environment, or the given variables, with status \f[CR]1\f[R]
if one is absent.
T}
T{
\f[CR]ps\f[R]
T}@T{
Lists processes with \f[CR]\-a\f[R], \f[CR]\-u\f[R], and \f[CR]\-x\f[R];
\f[CR]\-w\f[R] is accepted.
T}
T{
\f[CR]readlink\f[R], \f[CR]realpath\f[R] 
T}@T{
Prints the target of each symbolic link, with status \f[CR]1\f[R] for a
non\-link (\f[CR]readlink\f[R];
\f[CR]\-f\f[R]/\f[CR]\-\-canonicalize\f[R],
\f[CR]\-e\f[R]/\f[CR]\-\-canonicalize\-existing\f[R],
\f[CR]\-m\f[R]/\f[CR]\-\-canonicalize\-missing\f[R] print the canonical
absolute path with every link resolved as \f[CR]realpath\f[R] does
without a flag, with \f[CR]\-e\f[R], and with \f[CR]\-m\f[R], the last
of the three wins; \f[CR]\-n\f[R]/\f[CR]\-\-no\-newline\f[R] omit the
newline for a single file;
\f[CR]\-q\f[R]/\f[CR]\-\-quiet\f[R]/\f[CR]\-s\f[R]/\f[CR]\-\-silent\f[R]
suppress errors; \f[CR]\-z\f[R]/\f[CR]\-\-zero\f[R] end entries with
NUL); prints the canonical absolute path (\f[CR]realpath\f[R]; every
component but the last must exist, all with \f[CR]\-e\f[R], none with
\f[CR]\-m\f[R]; links resolve as met or with
\f[CR]\-P\f[R]/\f[CR]\-\-physical\f[R],
\f[CR]\-L\f[R]/\f[CR]\-\-logical\f[R] resolves \f[CR]..\f[R] first,
\f[CR]\-s\f[R]/\f[CR]\-\-no\-symlinks\f[R] and \f[CR]\-\-strip\f[R]
leave links alone, the last of the three wins;
\f[CR]\-\-relative\-to\f[R] prints paths relative to a directory,
\f[CR]\-\-relative\-base\f[R] prints paths below a directory relative to
it and others absolute, and with both, paths are relative to the first
when it is below the base; \f[CR]\-q\f[R]/\f[CR]\-\-quiet\f[R] omit
errors; \f[CR]\-z\f[R]/\f[CR]\-\-zero\f[R] end entries with NUL).
T}
T{
\f[CR]rm\f[R], \f[CR]unlink\f[R] 
T}@T{
Removes paths (\f[CR]\-r\f[R]/\f[CR]\-R\f[R]/\f[CR]\-\-recursive\f[R]
directories and contents, \f[CR]\-d\f[R]/\f[CR]\-\-dir\f[R] empty
directories, \f[CR]\-f\f[R]/\f[CR]\-\-force\f[R] ignore missing paths
without asking, \f[CR]\-i\f[R] ask before each removal, \f[CR]\-I\f[R]
ask once before removing more than three paths or a tree,
\f[CR]\-\-interactive=never|once|always\f[R],
\f[CR]\-v\f[R]/\f[CR]\-\-verbose\f[R] print each removed path,
\f[CR]\-\-dry\-run\f[R] print what would be removed and remove nothing,
\f[CR]\-x\f[R]/\f[CR]\-\-one\-file\-system\f[R] skip directories on
other file systems with status \f[CR]1\f[R]).
Refuses \f[CR].\f[R], \f[CR]..\f[R], and every spelling of a root
directory or a Windows drive root unless
\f[CR]\-\-no\-preserve\-root\f[R] is given;
\f[CR]\-\-preserve\-root=all\f[R] also refuses an operand on another
device than its parent.
A missing path returns \f[CR]1\f[R] without \f[CR]\-f\f[R].
\f[CR]unlink\f[R] removes one non\-directory path.
T}
T{
\f[CR]sed\f[R]
T}@T{
Applies an editing script, from the first operand or from each
\f[CR]\-e\f[R]/\f[CR]\-\-expression\f[R] and
\f[CR]\-f\f[R]/\f[CR]\-\-file\f[R], to the lines of each file or
standard input (\f[CR]\-n\f[R]/\f[CR]\-\-quiet\f[R] suppress automatic
printing, \f[CR]\-E\f[R]/\f[CR]\-\-extended\-regexp\f[R] extended
regular expressions).
Commands: \f[CR]s\f[R] with the \f[CR]g\f[R] and \f[CR]p\f[R] flags,
\f[CR]y\f[R], \f[CR]d\f[R], \f[CR]p\f[R], \f[CR]q\f[R], \f[CR]=\f[R],
and \f[CR]a\f[R]/\f[CR]i\f[R]/\f[CR]c\f[R] (text on the same line or on
the next lines after a backslash), with line, \f[CR]$\f[R], and regex
addresses and ranges.
Hold space, branch, and block commands are unsupported and return
\f[CR]1\f[R]; \f[CR]\-i\f[R] is an unknown flag with status
\f[CR]2\f[R].
T}
T{
\f[CR]seq\f[R]
T}@T{
Prints numbers with a nonzero step
(\f[CR]\-w\f[R]/\f[CR]\-\-equal\-width\f[R] pad with zeros,
\f[CR]\-s\f[R]/\f[CR]\-\-separator\f[R] separator,
\f[CR]\-f\f[R]/\f[CR]\-\-format\f[R] apply one printf \f[CR]%e\f[R],
\f[CR]%f\f[R], \f[CR]%g\f[R], or \f[CR]%a\f[R] conversion; excludes
\f[CR]\-w\f[R]).
Integers print exactly, and decimal, exponent, and hexadecimal operands
print with the most fraction digits of the first operand and the step.
T}
T{
\f[CR]sleep\f[R], \f[CR]timeout\f[R], \f[CR]watch\f[R]  
T}@T{
Pauses for the sum of the durations, with optional \f[CR]s\f[R],
\f[CR]m\f[R], \f[CR]h\f[R], or \f[CR]d\f[R] suffixes (\f[CR]sleep\f[R]);
runs a command with a time limit and an optional duration suffix
(\f[CR]timeout\f[R]; \f[CR]\-s\f[R]/\f[CR]\-\-signal\f[R] signal,
\f[CR]\-k\f[R]/\f[CR]\-\-kill\-after\f[R] send \f[CR]KILL\f[R] after a
further duration, \f[CR]\-p\f[R]/\f[CR]\-\-preserve\-status\f[R] return
the command status; returns \f[CR]124\f[R] on timeout and \f[CR]127\f[R]
when the command is not found); runs a command at an interval
(\f[CR]watch\f[R]; \f[CR]\-n\f[R] interval, \f[CR]\-t\f[R] omit the
title, \f[CR]\-g\f[R] exit when output changes, \f[CR]\-e\f[R] exit
after a command error, \f[CR]\-x\f[R] accepted).
On a terminal, \f[CR]q\f[R] or an interrupt exits \f[CR]watch\f[R] with
status \f[CR]0\f[R], and the command reads cooked terminal input.
T}
T{
\f[CR]sort\f[R]
T}@T{
Sorts lines by byte order or by \f[CR]\-k\f[R] keys of the form
\f[CR]F[.C][bdfghiMnrV][,F[.C][bdfghiMnrV]]\f[R] (\f[CR]\-t\f[R]
separator, \f[CR]\-b\f[R] ignore leading blanks, \f[CR]\-d\f[R] compare
only blanks and alphanumerics, \f[CR]\-f\f[R] fold case, \f[CR]\-i\f[R]
compare only printable characters, \f[CR]\-n\f[R] compare numbers,
\f[CR]\-r\f[R] reverse, \f[CR]\-g\f[R] compare floating numbers
including exponents, infinities, and NaN with text first, \f[CR]\-h\f[R]
compare numbers with
\f[CR]K\f[R]/\f[CR]M\f[R]/\f[CR]G\f[R]/\f[CR]T\f[R]/\f[CR]P\f[R]/\f[CR]E\f[R]/\f[CR]Z\f[R]/\f[CR]Y\f[R]/\f[CR]R\f[R]/\f[CR]Q\f[R]
suffixes, \f[CR]\-M\f[R] compare month abbreviations with other text
first, \f[CR]\-V\f[R] compare version numbers, \f[CR]\-z\f[R] NUL line
ends, \f[CR]\-u\f[R] keep the first of equal keys, \f[CR]\-c\f[R] report
the first unsorted line, \f[CR]\-C\f[R] report only the status,
\f[CR]\-o\f[R] write to a file, \f[CR]\-s\f[R] skip the last\-resort
whole\-line comparison, \f[CR]\-m\f[R] accepted).
At most one of \f[CR]\-g\f[R], \f[CR]\-h\f[R], \f[CR]\-M\f[R], and
\f[CR]\-n\f[R] applies to a key, and none combines with \f[CR]\-d\f[R],
\f[CR]\-i\f[R], or \f[CR]\-V\f[R].
T}
T{
\f[CR]split\f[R]
T}@T{
Splits a file or standard input into pieces \f[CR]xaa\f[R],
\f[CR]xab\f[R], and so on (or with the prefix operand) of
\f[CR]1000\f[R] lines, \f[CR]\-l\f[R]/\f[CR]\-\-lines\f[R] lines, or
\f[CR]\-b\f[R]/\f[CR]\-\-bytes\f[R] bytes
(\f[CR]\-a\f[R]/\f[CR]\-\-suffix\-length\f[R] number of suffix letters).
Returns \f[CR]1\f[R] for a count of \f[CR]0\f[R].
T}
T{
\f[CR]stat\f[R]
T}@T{
Prints file or file system metadata (\f[CR]\-L\f[R] follow links,
\f[CR]\-f\f[R] file system, \f[CR]\-t\f[R] terse output, \f[CR]\-c\f[R]
apply a format, \f[CR]\-\-printf\f[R] apply a format without a trailing
newline).
T}
T{
\f[CR]strings\f[R]
T}@T{
Prints each run of at least \f[CR]4\f[R] printable characters in each
file or standard input (\f[CR]\-n\f[R]/\f[CR]\-\-bytes\f[R] minimum
length, \f[CR]\-t\f[R]/\f[CR]\-\-radix\f[R] prefix each string with its
offset in \f[CR]d\f[R], \f[CR]o\f[R], or \f[CR]x\f[R],
\f[CR]\-a\f[R]/\f[CR]\-\-all\f[R] scan the whole file).
T}
T{
\f[CR]stty\f[R], \f[CR]tabs\f[R], \f[CR]tput\f[R], \f[CR]tty\f[R]   
T}@T{
Reports or changes terminal settings (\f[CR]stty\f[R]; \f[CR]\-a\f[R]
report all, \f[CR]\-g\f[R] print a state that restores them later); sets
the terminal tab stops to every \f[CR]8\f[R] columns, every N columns
for \f[CR]\-N\f[R], or the listed columns by writing escape sequences to
standard output (\f[CR]tabs\f[R]); writes the escape sequence of a
terminal capability from a fixed table (\f[CR]tput\f[R]; \f[CR]cols\f[R]
and \f[CR]lines\f[R] print the terminal size and need a terminal,
\f[CR]longname\f[R] prints the description of \f[CR]TERM\f[R] or of
\f[CR]\-T\f[R]/\f[CR]\-\-terminal\f[R], an unknown capability returns
\f[CR]1\f[R]); prints the terminal of standard input, or
\f[CR]not a tty\f[R] with status \f[CR]1\f[R] (\f[CR]tty\f[R];
\f[CR]\-s\f[R]/\f[CR]\-\-silent\f[R] print nothing).
See the \f[CR]tput\f[R] bullet below the table.
T}
T{
\f[CR]sync\f[R]
T}@T{
Flushes file system data (\f[CR]\-d\f[R] the data of each operand,
\f[CR]\-f\f[R] the file system of each operand, or every file system
without one).
T}
T{
\f[CR]tee\f[R]
T}@T{
Copies standard input to standard output and to files, appending with
\f[CR]\-a\f[R].
T}
T{
\f[CR]touch\f[R]
T}@T{
Updates file times (\f[CR]\-a\f[R] access time, \f[CR]\-c\f[R] skip
missing files, \f[CR]\-m\f[R] modification time, \f[CR]\-r\f[R] copy a
reference file, \f[CR]\-t\f[R] set a timestamp).
T}
T{
\f[CR]tr\f[R]
T}@T{
Translates bytes with ranges, classes, \f[CR][=c=]\f[R] equivalence
classes, and \f[CR][c*n]\f[R] repeats (\f[CR]\-d\f[R] delete,
\f[CR]\-c\f[R]/\f[CR]\-C\f[R] complement the first set, \f[CR]\-s\f[R]
squeeze runs of a byte from the last set,
\f[CR]\-t\f[R]/\f[CR]\-\-truncate\-set1\f[R] truncate the first set
instead of padding the shorter second set with its last byte).
When translating, the second set accepts only \f[CR][:upper:]\f[R] and
\f[CR][:lower:]\f[R], each aligned with an \f[CR][:upper:]\f[R] or
\f[CR][:lower:]\f[R] class in the first set, and one \f[CR][c*]\f[R]
repeat that fills it to the length of the first; a \f[CR][c*]\f[R] in
the first set is an error.
T}
T{
\f[CR]tsort\f[R]
T}@T{
Prints a total order of the pairs of words in a file or standard input.
A cycle prints a partial order and returns \f[CR]1\f[R].
T}
T{
\f[CR]uname\f[R]
T}@T{
Prints the system name, or the fields of \f[CR]\-m\f[R] (machine),
\f[CR]\-n\f[R] (node), \f[CR]\-r\f[R] (release), \f[CR]\-s\f[R]
(system), and \f[CR]\-v\f[R] (version), or all of them with
\f[CR]\-a\f[R].
T}
T{
\f[CR]uniq\f[R]
T}@T{
Collapses adjacent equal lines (\f[CR]\-c\f[R] count, \f[CR]\-d\f[R]
only repeated lines, \f[CR]\-u\f[R] only unique lines, \f[CR]\-D\f[R]
every line of a repeated run, \f[CR]\-f\f[R]/\f[CR]\-s\f[R] skip
fields/characters, \f[CR]\-w\f[R] compare at most N characters,
\f[CR]\-i\f[R] ignore ASCII case,
\f[CR]\-\-all\-repeated[=none|prepend|separate]\f[R] act as
\f[CR]\-D\f[R] with empty lines before or between runs,
\f[CR]\-\-group[=separate|prepend|append|both]\f[R] print every line
with empty lines between, before, or after runs and exclude
\f[CR]\-c\f[R], \f[CR]\-d\f[R], \f[CR]\-D\f[R], and \f[CR]\-u\f[R],
\f[CR]\-z\f[R] NUL line ends).
A second operand is the output file.
T}
T{
\f[CR]wc\f[R]
T}@T{
Counts lines (\f[CR]\-l\f[R]), words (\f[CR]\-w\f[R]), characters
(\f[CR]\-m\f[R]), and bytes (\f[CR]\-c\f[R]).
T}
T{
\f[CR]which\f[R]
T}@T{
Resolves builtins, \f[CR]PATH\f[R] programs, and bundled utilities, with
\f[CR]\-a\f[R]/\f[CR]\-\-all\f[R] and
\f[CR]\-q\f[R]/\f[CR]\-\-quiet\f[R].
T}
T{
\f[CR]xargs\f[R]
T}@T{
Appends arguments from standard input to a command, which reads the null
device (\f[CR]\-a\f[R]/\f[CR]\-\-arg\-file\f[R] read arguments from a
file and leave the command standard input, \f[CR]\-0\f[R] split on NUL,
\f[CR]\-d\f[R]/\f[CR]\-\-delimiter\f[R] split on one character or escape
such as \f[CR]\[rs]n\f[R], \f[CR]\[rs]t\f[R], \f[CR]\[rs]x41\f[R], or
\f[CR]\[rs]0\f[R], both keeping quotes and backslashes literal and
disabling the end marker, \f[CR]\-r\f[R] skip an empty input,
\f[CR]\-E\f[R] set the end marker,
\f[CR]\-e[EOF]\f[R]/\f[CR]\-\-eof[=EOF]\f[R] set or remove it,
\f[CR]\-I\f[R] replace a string with each input line,
\f[CR]\-i[R]\f[R]/\f[CR]\-\-replace[=R]\f[R] replace \f[CR]R\f[R] or
\f[CR]{}\f[R], \f[CR]\-L\f[R]/\f[CR]\-n\f[R]/\f[CR]\-s\f[R] limit each
command to lines/arguments/bytes,
\f[CR]\-P\f[R]/\f[CR]\-\-max\-procs\f[R] run that many commands at once
or as many as possible for \f[CR]0\f[R] with output that may interleave,
\f[CR]\-p\f[R] ask on the terminal before each command, \f[CR]\-t\f[R]
trace, \f[CR]\-x\f[R] fail when a command does not fit).
For \f[CR]\-L\f[R], empty lines do not count and a trailing blank
continues a line.
Returns \f[CR]123\f[R] when a command fails, \f[CR]124\f[R] when one
exits with \f[CR]255\f[R], \f[CR]125\f[R] when a signal ends one, and
\f[CR]126\f[R] or \f[CR]127\f[R] when one cannot run, which under
\f[CR]\-P\f[R] stops the run after the running commands finish.
T}
T{
\f[CR]yes\f[R]
T}@T{
Repeats the joined operands, or \f[CR]y\f[R], until output closes.
T}
.TE
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[B]\f[CB]grep\f[B] colors\f[R] \- \f[CR]GREP_COLORS\f[R] holds
colon\-separated GNU capabilities such as \f[CR]ms=01;31\f[R].
The capabilities \f[CR]ms\f[R], \f[CR]mt\f[R], \f[CR]sl\f[R],
\f[CR]cx\f[R], \f[CR]fn\f[R], \f[CR]ln\f[R], \f[CR]se\f[R], and
\f[CR]rv\f[R] apply, unknown ones are ignored, and an empty value turns
that color off.
\f[CR]GREP_COLOR\f[R] sets the match color below \f[CR]GREP_COLORS\f[R].
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[B]\f[CB]less\f[B] keys\f[R] \- The keys come from the terminal.
.RS 2
.IP \[bu] 2
Movement: Space, \f[CR]f\f[R], Ctrl\-F, Ctrl\-V, and Page Down move
forward a page; \f[CR]b\f[R], Ctrl\-B, and Page Up back a page;
\f[CR]d\f[R] and Ctrl\-D forward half a page; \f[CR]u\f[R] and Ctrl\-U
back half a page; \f[CR]j\f[R], \f[CR]e\f[R], Enter, Down, Ctrl\-E, and
Ctrl\-N one row down; \f[CR]k\f[R], \f[CR]y\f[R], Up, Ctrl\-P, and
Ctrl\-Y one row up.
The mouse wheel scrolls three rows.
\f[CR]g\f[R], \f[CR]<\f[R], and Home go to the top; \f[CR]G\f[R],
\f[CR]>\f[R], and End go to the bottom; \f[CR]r\f[R] and Ctrl\-L redraw.
.IP \[bu] 2
Search: \f[CR]/PATTERN\f[R] and \f[CR]?PATTERN\f[R] search forward and
backward, and \f[CR]n\f[R] and \f[CR]N\f[R] repeat the search.
An empty pattern repeats the previous one, Escape cancels the prompt,
and an invalid pattern is reported.
.IP \[bu] 2
Status row \- Shows the file, the visible lines and their total, the
position, and \f[CR](END)\f[R] at the end.
.RE
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[B]\f[CB]more\f[B] keys\f[R] \- Space and \f[CR]f\f[R] show the next
page; Enter, \f[CR]j\f[R], and Down the next line; \f[CR]d\f[R] half a
page; \f[CR]b\f[R], \f[CR]k\f[R], Page Up, and Up go further back;
\f[CR]g\f[R] and \f[CR]G\f[R] go to the top and the bottom; the searches
of \f[CR]less\f[R] apply; \f[CR]q\f[R], or a forward key at the end,
quits.
The status row shows \f[CR]\-\-More\-\-\f[R] and the position, or
\f[CR](END)\f[R].
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[B]\f[CB]make\f[B] syntax\f[R] \- Functions: \f[CR]abspath\f[R],
\f[CR]addprefix\f[R], \f[CR]addsuffix\f[R], \f[CR]and\f[R],
\f[CR]basename\f[R], \f[CR]call\f[R], \f[CR]dir\f[R], \f[CR]error\f[R],
\f[CR]eval\f[R], \f[CR]filter\f[R], \f[CR]filter\-out\f[R],
\f[CR]findstring\f[R], \f[CR]firstword\f[R], \f[CR]flavor\f[R],
\f[CR]foreach\f[R], \f[CR]if\f[R], \f[CR]join\f[R], \f[CR]lastword\f[R],
\f[CR]notdir\f[R], \f[CR]or\f[R], \f[CR]origin\f[R],
\f[CR]patsubst\f[R], \f[CR]realpath\f[R], \f[CR]shell\f[R],
\f[CR]sort\f[R], \f[CR]strip\f[R], \f[CR]subst\f[R], \f[CR]suffix\f[R],
\f[CR]value\f[R], \f[CR]warning\f[R], \f[CR]wildcard\f[R],
\f[CR]word\f[R], \f[CR]wordlist\f[R], and \f[CR]words\f[R].
Directives: \f[CR]include\f[R], \f[CR]ifeq\f[R], \f[CR]ifneq\f[R],
\f[CR]ifdef\f[R], \f[CR]ifndef\f[R], \f[CR]else\f[R], \f[CR]endif\f[R],
\f[CR]define\f[R], \f[CR]override\f[R], \f[CR]export\f[R], and
\f[CR]unexport\f[R].
Special targets: \f[CR].DEFAULT\f[R], \f[CR].IGNORE\f[R],
\f[CR].PHONY\f[R], \f[CR].POSIX\f[R], \f[CR].PRECIOUS\f[R],
\f[CR].SCCS_GET\f[R], \f[CR].SILENT\f[R], and \f[CR].SUFFIXES\f[R].
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[B]\f[CB]tput\f[B] capabilities\f[R] \- \f[CR]bel\f[R],
\f[CR]blink\f[R], \f[CR]bold\f[R], \f[CR]civis\f[R], \f[CR]clear\f[R],
\f[CR]cnorm\f[R], \f[CR]cub1\f[R], \f[CR]cud1\f[R], \f[CR]cuf1\f[R],
\f[CR]cuu1\f[R], \f[CR]dch1\f[R], \f[CR]dl1\f[R], \f[CR]ed\f[R],
\f[CR]el\f[R], \f[CR]home\f[R], \f[CR]ich1\f[R], \f[CR]il1\f[R],
\f[CR]ind\f[R], \f[CR]init\f[R], \f[CR]reset\f[R], \f[CR]rev\f[R],
\f[CR]rmso\f[R], \f[CR]rmul\f[R], \f[CR]sgr0\f[R], \f[CR]smso\f[R],
\f[CR]smul\f[R], and \f[CR]cup\f[R] with a row and a column.
.SS Windows platform semantics
On Windows, Koshka executes the exact same shell grammar with the
following OS adaptations:
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[B]Virtual path translation\f[R] \- \f[CR]/dev/null\f[R] maps to the
Windows \f[CR]NUL\f[R] device (\f[CR]compatibility.dev_null=on\f[R]),
and \f[CR]/tmp\f[R] (or paths beneath \f[CR]/tmp\f[R]) maps to
\f[CR]$TEMP\f[R] (\f[CR]compatibility.slash_tmp=on\f[R]).
Both options are on by default.
Bash startup files retain their POSIX paths.
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[B]Environment and process model\f[R] \- Environment variable
identifiers are case\-insensitive, individual exported values truncate
at \f[CR]32,766\f[R] UTF\-16 code units, \f[CR]PATH\f[R] (or
\f[CR]Path\f[R]) uses \f[CR];\f[R] delimiters (ignoring empty segments),
and user configuration falls back to \f[CR]$USERPROFILE\f[R] when
\f[CR]$HOME\f[R] is unset.
Subshells spawn in new OS processes, and background jobs run in
dedicated console process groups.
Process substitutions (\f[CR]<(...)\f[R], \f[CR]>(...)\f[R]) use
FIFO\-like pipes where sequential readers continue from the prior read
offset and sequential writers append to the stream.
See Process substitution, \f[CR]echo\f[R], \f[CR]pwd \-W\f[R], and local
\f[CR]assimilate\f[R] for more Windows behavior.
