T{
Variable
T}@T{
Behavior
T}
_
T{
\f[CR]BASH\f[R], \f[CR]BASH_VERSION\f[R], \f[CR]BASH_VERSINFO\f[R]
T}@T{
Hold the Bash identity, set only in \f[CR]bash\f[R] and
\f[CR]bash\-posix\f[R] or in a session that initialized one of them
(\f[CR]BASH\f[R] is the executable, \f[CR]BASH_VERSION\f[R] is
\f[CR]5.3.0(1)\-kosh\f[R], \f[CR]BASH_VERSINFO\f[R] holds the version
fields with the build host in element 5).
T}
T{
\f[CR]BASH_ALIASES\f[R]
T}@T{
Holds the aliases (assigning an element defines an alias, unsetting an
element does nothing, unsetting the array disconnects it).
T}
T{
\f[CR]BASH_ARGC\f[R], \f[CR]BASH_ARGV\f[R]
T}@T{
Hold the argument count of each recorded frame and the arguments in
reverse order, innermost first.
The \f[CR]extdebug\f[R] option records function and source calls in
them.
Without it, \f[CR]BASH_ARGV\f[R] is empty and \f[CR]BASH_ARGC\f[R] holds
one \f[CR]0\f[R] outside functions and is empty inside them.
Assignments do nothing, and \f[CR]unset\f[R] and \f[CR]local\f[R] fail.
T}
T{
\f[CR]BASH_ARGV0\f[R]
T}@T{
Holds argument zero of the shell (assignment does not change
\f[CR]$0\f[R]).
T}
T{
\f[CR]BASH_COMMAND\f[R]
T}@T{
Holds the command that is running or about to run.
T}
T{
\f[CR]BASH_EXECUTION_STRING\f[R]
T}@T{
Holds the command string of \f[CR]\-c\f[R].
T}
T{
\f[CR]BASH_LINENO\f[R], \f[CR]BASH_SOURCE\f[R], \f[CR]FUNCNAME\f[R]
T}@T{
Hold the call stack: \f[CR]FUNCNAME[0]\f[R] is the running function,
\f[CR]BASH_SOURCE[i]\f[R] the file that defines \f[CR]FUNCNAME[i]\f[R],
and \f[CR]BASH_LINENO[i]\f[R] the line where \f[CR]FUNCNAME[i]\f[R] was
called.
Empty in the \f[CR]sh\f[R] mood.
T}
T{
\f[CR]BASH_MONOSECONDS\f[R]
T}@T{
Holds a monotonic clock in milliseconds.
T}
T{
\f[CR]BASH_REMATCH\f[R]
T}@T{
Holds the match and groups of the last successful
\f[CR][[ =\[ti] ]]\f[R], and is empty after a failed match.
T}
T{
\f[CR]BASH_SUBSHELL\f[R]
T}@T{
Holds the subshell depth (\f[CR]0\f[R] in the shell).
T}
T{
\f[CR]BASHOPTS\f[R]
T}@T{
Holds the read\-only, colon\-separated list of \f[CR]shopt\f[R] options
that are on; an environment value is ignored.
T}
T{
\f[CR]BASHPID\f[R]
T}@T{
Holds the process id of the current shell or subshell.
T}
T{
\f[CR]COMP_CWORD\f[R], \f[CR]COMP_LINE\f[R], \f[CR]COMP_POINT\f[R],
\f[CR]COMP_WORDS\f[R]
T}@T{
Hold the cursor word index, line, cursor byte offset, and words for a
completion function (see \f[CR]complete\f[R]); \f[CR]COMP_KEY\f[R] and
\f[CR]COMP_TYPE\f[R] are exported to a \f[CR]complete \-C\f[R] command
only.
T}
T{
\f[CR]COPROC\f[R], \f[CR]COPROC_PID\f[R]
T}@T{
Hold the descriptors and process of a coprocess without \f[CR]NAME\f[R].
T}
T{
\f[CR]DIRSTACK\f[R]
T}@T{
Holds the current directory followed by the saved stack.
Assigning an existing index other than \f[CR]0\f[R] changes that entry;
other assignments and element unsets do nothing, and unsetting the array
disconnects it.
T}
T{
\f[CR]EPOCHREALTIME\f[R], \f[CR]EPOCHSECONDS\f[R]
T}@T{
Hold the wall time in seconds (\f[CR]EPOCHREALTIME\f[R] with
microseconds).
T}
T{
\f[CR]EUID\f[R], \f[CR]UID\f[R]
T}@T{
Hold the read\-only effective and real user ids.
T}
T{
\f[CR]GROUPS\f[R]
T}@T{
Holds the real group id.
T}
T{
\f[CR]HISTCMD\f[R]
T}@T{
Holds the history number of the current command (\f[CR]0\f[R] in a
non\-interactive shell).
T}
T{
\f[CR]HOSTNAME\f[R], \f[CR]HOSTTYPE\f[R], \f[CR]MACHTYPE\f[R],
\f[CR]OSTYPE\f[R]
T}@T{
Hold the host and platform.
T}
T{
\f[CR]LINENO\f[R]
T}@T{
Holds the line of the running command; each command in a multi\-line
command substitution reports its own file line.
Assignments are discarded, and \f[CR]unset\f[R] does not remove the
behavior.
T}
T{
\f[CR]MAPFILE\f[R]
T}@T{
Holds the default array of \f[CR]mapfile\f[R].
T}
T{
\f[CR]OLDPWD\f[R], \f[CR]PWD\f[R]
T}@T{
Hold the previous and current logical working directories, updated by
\f[CR]cd\f[R], and are exported only when inherited exported or exported
explicitly.
A logical \f[CR]PWD\f[R] is accepted at startup only when absolute and
identifying the current directory.
T}
T{
\f[CR]OPTARG\f[R], \f[CR]OPTIND\f[R]
T}@T{
Hold the argument of the last option and the index of the next argument
for \f[CR]getopts\f[R] (\f[CR]OPTIND\f[R] starts at \f[CR]1\f[R]).
T}
T{
\f[CR]PIPESTATUS\f[R]
T}@T{
Holds the status of each stage of the last foreground pipeline.
T}
T{
\f[CR]PPID\f[R]
T}@T{
Holds the parent process id (read\-only except in the \f[CR]sh\f[R]
mood).
T}
T{
\f[CR]RANDOM\f[R]
T}@T{
Yields a random integer from \f[CR]0\f[R] to \f[CR]32767\f[R].
Assignment seeds the sequence reproducibly, and \f[CR]unset\f[R] makes
it an ordinary variable.
T}
T{
\f[CR]REPLY\f[R]
T}@T{
Holds the line read by \f[CR]read\f[R] without a variable and by
\f[CR]select\f[R].
T}
T{
\f[CR]SECONDS\f[R]
T}@T{
Holds the seconds since the shell started.
Assignment moves the base, and \f[CR]unset\f[R] makes it an ordinary
variable.
T}
T{
\f[CR]SHELLOPTS\f[R]
T}@T{
Holds the read\-only, colon\-separated list of \f[CR]set \-o\f[R]
options that are on; an environment value is ignored.
T}
T{
\f[CR]SHLVL\f[R]
T}@T{
Holds the shell nesting level, incremented at startup (a negative
inherited value becomes \f[CR]1\f[R], and an inherited value of
\f[CR]1000\f[R] or more restarts at \f[CR]1\f[R]).
T}
T{
\f[CR]SRANDOM\f[R]
T}@T{
Yields a random 32\-bit integer from the system generator.
T}
.TE
.SS Variables that affect the shell
.PP
