T{
\f[CR]BASH_COMPLETION_VERSINFO\f[R]
T}@T{
Suppresses sourcing of the bash\-completion script in an interactive
\f[CR]bash\f[R] mood shell when set.
T}
T{
\f[CR]BASH_ENV\f[R], \f[CR]ENV\f[R]
T}@T{
Select startup files (see the startup table above); values undergo
parameter expansion and command substitution.
T}
T{
\f[CR]BASH_XTRACEFD\f[R]
T}@T{
Selects the descriptor that receives \f[CR]xtrace\f[R] output.
Standard error receives it when the variable is unset or not a
nonnegative integer; a closed descriptor discards it.
T}
T{
\f[CR]CDPATH\f[R]
T}@T{
Lists the colon\-separated directories that \f[CR]cd\f[R] searches for a
relative operand.
T}
T{
\f[CR]COLUMNS\f[R], \f[CR]LINES\f[R]
T}@T{
Hold the terminal size, set at the start of an interactive shell and not
updated when the terminal changes size.
T}
T{
\f[CR]FCEDIT\f[R], \f[CR]EDITOR\f[R], \f[CR]VISUAL\f[R]
T}@T{
Select editors: \f[CR]FCEDIT\f[R], then \f[CR]EDITOR\f[R] for
\f[CR]fc\f[R]; \f[CR]VISUAL\f[R], then \f[CR]EDITOR\f[R] for Ctrl\-X
Ctrl\-E.
T}
T{
\f[CR]GLOBIGNORE\f[R]
T}@T{
Lists colon\-separated patterns of pathname expansion results to remove
(see Pathname expansion).
T}
T{
\f[CR]HOME\f[R]
T}@T{
Holds the home directory used by \f[CR]cd\f[R] and tilde expansion (on
Windows the shell uses \f[CR]USERPROFILE\f[R] when \f[CR]HOME\f[R] is
unset).
T}
T{
\f[CR]IFS\f[R]
T}@T{
Holds the field separators and the joiner of \f[CR]\[dq]$*\[dq]\f[R], by
default space, tab, and newline; an environment value is ignored.
T}
T{
\f[CR]IGNOREEOF\f[R]
T}@T{
Sets the number of consecutive end\-of\-file inputs that an interactive
shell needs before it exits while \f[CR]ignoreeof\f[R] is on.
Enabling the option sets an unset \f[CR]IGNOREEOF\f[R] to \f[CR]10\f[R],
assigning \f[CR]IGNOREEOF\f[R] enables the option, and unsetting it
disables the option.
T}
T{
\f[CR]LANG\f[R], \f[CR]LC_ALL\f[R], \f[CR]LC_COLLATE\f[R],
\f[CR]LC_CTYPE\f[R], \f[CR]LC_NUMERIC\f[R]
T}@T{
Select the locale (see Locale).
T}
T{
\f[CR]MANPATH\f[R]
T}@T{
Lists the manual page directories that completion, hints, and
\f[CR]man\f[R] search.
T}
T{
\f[CR]NO_COLOR\f[R]
T}@T{
Disables color in the prompt, diagnostics, editor, and bundled utilities
when nonempty.
T}
T{
\f[CR]OPTERR\f[R]
T}@T{
Silences \f[CR]getopts\f[R] diagnostics when \f[CR]0\f[R].
T}
T{
\f[CR]PATH\f[R]
T}@T{
Lists the colon\-separated command search path.
An empty element, an empty value, and an unset \f[CR]PATH\f[R] search
the current directory.
The shell does not set \f[CR]PATH\f[R] when the environment lacks it.
On Windows the separator is a semicolon, an empty element is skipped,
and \f[CR]Path\f[R] counts as \f[CR]PATH\f[R].
T}
T{
\f[CR]PROMPT_COMMAND\f[R], \f[CR]PS0\f[R], \f[CR]PS1\f[R],
\f[CR]PS2\f[R], \f[CR]PS3\f[R], \f[CR]PS4\f[R], \f[CR]RPS1\f[R],
\f[CR]RPROMPT\f[R]
T}@T{
Hold the prompts and the command run before each prompt (see Prompt
rendering); \f[CR]PS3\f[R] is the \f[CR]select\f[R] prompt,
\f[CR]#? \f[R] by default.
T}
T{
\f[CR]SHELL\f[R]
T}@T{
Holds the user shell path.
An inherited value is kept, and an unset \f[CR]SHELL\f[R] becomes the
path of the executable.
T}
T{
\f[CR]TERM\f[R], \f[CR]COLORTERM\f[R], \f[CR]TERM_PROGRAM\f[R]
T}@T{
Describe terminal capabilities (see Interactive line editing);
\f[CR]TERM=dumb\f[R] disables color and the terminal integration marks.
T}
T{
\f[CR]TIMEFORMAT\f[R]
T}@T{
Selects the \f[CR]time\f[R] report format: \f[CR]%R\f[R], \f[CR]%U\f[R],
\f[CR]%S\f[R] are elapsed, user, and system seconds, \f[CR]%P\f[R] the
processor percentage, \f[CR]%3R\f[R] three decimals, \f[CR]%lR\f[R]
minutes and seconds, \f[CR]%%\f[R] a percent sign.
An empty value prints nothing, and an unset value selects the default
report.
T}
T{
\f[CR]TMPDIR\f[R]
T}@T{
Selects the directory for the temporary files of \f[CR]fc\f[R], Ctrl\-X
Ctrl\-E, and \f[CR]slurp\f[R].
The shell reads it from the environment, so an assignment needs
\f[CR]export\f[R]; an empty value is ignored, the default is
\f[CR]/tmp\f[R], and on Windows the directory is \f[CR]TEMP\f[R].
T}
T{
\f[CR]TZ\f[R]
T}@T{
Holds the time zone.
The shell uses the inherited value, so an assignment in the shell
changes the zone of later programs only.
T}
T{
\f[CR]XDG_CONFIG_HOME\f[R]
T}@T{
Sets the base of the user settings directory (see Startup and
configuration file loading); a relative or empty value is ignored.
T}
