\f[CR]MAIL\f[R], \f[CR]MAILCHECK\f[R], \f[CR]MAILPATH\f[R],
\f[CR]TMOUT\f[R], \f[CR]PROMPT_DIRTRIM\f[R], \f[CR]FIGNORE\f[R],
\f[CR]EXECIGNORE\f[R], \f[CR]HOSTFILE\f[R], \f[CR]INPUTRC\f[R],
\f[CR]CHILD_MAX\f[R], \f[CR]BASH_COMPAT\f[R],
\f[CR]BASH_LOADABLES_PATH\f[R], \f[CR]GLOBSORT\f[R],
\f[CR]FUNCNEST\f[R], \f[CR]auto_resume\f[R], and
\f[CR]POSIXLY_CORRECT\f[R].
.SS Word expansions, redirections, arithmetic, and conditionals
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[B]Expansion order\f[R] \- Brace expansion, tilde expansion, then
parameter expansion, arithmetic expansion, command substitution, and
process substitution from left to right, then field splitting, pathname
expansion, and quote removal.
Only brace expansion, field splitting, and pathname expansion can change
the number of words.
.SS Brace, tilde, process substitution, field splitting, and quote removal
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[B]Brace expansion\f[R] \- Unquoted \f[CR]{a,b,...}\f[R] produces one
word per item with the surrounding text (\f[CR]a{b,c}d\f[R] gives
\f[CR]abd\f[R] \f[CR]acd\f[R]; items may be empty; braces nest).
.RS 2
.IP \[bu] 2
Sequences \f[CR]{x..y}\f[R] and \f[CR]{x..y..step}\f[R] produce integers
or single characters from \f[CR]x\f[R] to \f[CR]y\f[R] (a leading zero
on either integer pads every result to one width, step \f[CR]0\f[R]
counts as \f[CR]1\f[R], the sign of the step is ignored, character
ranges include every character between the ends as in
\f[CR]{Z..a}\f[R]).
.IP \[bu] 2
An invalid list or sequence (\f[CR]{a}\f[R], \f[CR]{a\-z}\f[R],
\f[CR]{1..a}\f[R]) and a sequence that holds an expansion stay literal.
.IP \[bu] 2
Does not apply in an assignment value, here\-string, \f[CR]case\f[R]
pattern, or redirection target; off in \f[CR]sh\f[R] and while
\f[CR]braceexpand\f[R] is off.
.RE
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[B]Tilde expansion\f[R] \- An unquoted leading \f[CR]\[ti]\f[R]
expands to \f[CR]HOME\f[R], \f[CR]\[ti]user\f[R] to the home directory
of \f[CR]user\f[R], \f[CR]\[ti]+\f[R] to \f[CR]PWD\f[R],
\f[CR]\[ti]\-\f[R] to \f[CR]OLDPWD\f[R].
The prefix ends at the first slash.
.RS 2
.IP \[bu] 2
Unknown users, \f[CR]\[ti]\-\f[R] with \f[CR]OLDPWD\f[R] unset, and the
directory stack forms \f[CR]\[ti]N\f[R], \f[CR]\[ti]+N\f[R],
\f[CR]\[ti]\-N\f[R] stay literal.
An empty \f[CR]HOME\f[R] expands to an empty word, and an unset
\f[CR]HOME\f[R] is an error.
.IP \[bu] 2
Also expands after \f[CR]=\f[R] and \f[CR]:\f[R] in assignments and in
the words of \f[CR]export\f[R], \f[CR]declare\f[R], \f[CR]local\f[R],
\f[CR]readonly\f[R], and (outside \f[CR]sh\f[R]) in any argument that
looks like an assignment such as \f[CR]a=\[ti]\f[R].
.RE
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[B]Process substitution\f[R] \- \f[CR]<(command)\f[R] and
\f[CR]>(command)\f[R] expand to a path that reads the output of
\f[CR]command\f[R] or writes its input, with \f[CR]command\f[R] in a
separate process.
Expands anywhere in an unquoted word (\f[CR]p=<(command)\f[R] assigns
the path) in every mood.
.RS 2
.IP \[bu] 2
The path stays open until the expanding command finishes (for a
\f[CR]for\f[R] word list, until the loop finishes); the shell then
closes it and waits for the process.
.IP \[bu] 2
Sets \f[CR]$!\f[R] to the process, and \f[CR]wait\f[R] on it returns its
status.
.IP \[bu] 2
POSIX path is \f[CR]/dev/fd/63\f[R] or the next free descriptor above
it.
On Windows it is a FIFO\-like pipe: each reader continues where the
previous stopped and each writer appends to the same stream.
.RE
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[B]Field splitting\f[R] \- Results of unquoted parameter expansion,
command substitution, and arithmetic expansion split at the bytes of
\f[CR]IFS\f[R].
A run of \f[CR]IFS\f[R] whitespace collapses and is ignored at both
ends, each other \f[CR]IFS\f[R] byte delimits a possibly empty field,
and an empty \f[CR]IFS\f[R] disables splitting.
An unquoted expansion that yields nothing produces no field, and
\f[CR]\[dq]\[dq]\f[R] produces an empty field.
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[B]Quote removal\f[R] \- Removes unquoted backslashes, single quotes,
and double quotes that did not result from an expansion.
.SS Parameter and substitution forms
.PP
.TS
