.TE
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[B]Numbers\f[R] \- Decimal, octal (leading \f[CR]0\f[R]), hexadecimal
(\f[CR]0x\f[R]), binary (\f[CR]0b\f[R]), or base \f[CR]b\f[R] from
\f[CR]2\f[R] to \f[CR]64\f[R] as \f[CR]b#digits\f[R] (digits beyond
\f[CR]9\f[R] come from letters, \f[CR]\[at]\f[R], \f[CR]_\f[R]).
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[B]Variables\f[R] \- A variable is replaced by its value, which is
evaluated as an expression in turn (\f[CR]x=1+2\f[R] makes
\f[CR]x*2\f[R] equal \f[CR]6\f[R]).
An empty value counts as \f[CR]0\f[R], and \f[CR]$\f[R] or a backquote
inside a value is an error.
A subscript taken from a value is expanded again (with
\f[CR]q=\[aq]a[$i]\[aq]\f[R], \f[CR]$((q))\f[R] is the element at
\f[CR]i\f[R]).
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[B]Quotes\f[R] \- Outside \f[CR]sh\f[R], double quotes inside
\f[CR]$(( ))\f[R], \f[CR](( ))\f[R], a C\-style \f[CR]for\f[R] header, a
subscript, or a substring offset are removed first
(\f[CR]$(( \[dq]1 + 2\[dq] * 3 ))\f[R] is \f[CR]7\f[R]).
\f[CR]sh\f[R] rejects every quote there.
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[B]Errors\f[R] \- Division by zero, an invalid digit, a missing
operand, an unexpected token, and a negative shift count are errors
(termination per mood under Error termination matrix across moods).
Shifts, bitwise operators, and the exponent need integers, and division
of two integers is integer division.
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[B]Precision\f[R] \-
\f[CR]interpreter.arithmetic_uses_big_numbers\f[R]
(\f[CR]\-\-enable\-extended\-arithmetic\f[R], on in the \f[CR]kosh\f[R]
mood) selects arbitrary\-precision integers and finite decimals
(\f[CR]$((2**100))\f[R] is exact; \f[CR]$((7.0/2))\f[R] is
\f[CR]3.5\f[R]).
Without it arithmetic uses wrapping 64\-bit signed integers.
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[B]Unset variables\f[R] \- An unset variable in an expression is an
error in the \f[CR]kosh\f[R] mood and evaluates as \f[CR]0\f[R] in the
compatibility moods.
.SS Conditional expressions (\f[CR][[ ]]\f[R], \f[CR]test\f[R], \f[CR][ ]\f[R])
.PP
.TS
