T}
.TE
.SS Word designators
A colon separates a designator from the event and may be omitted before
\f[CR]\[ha]\f[R], \f[CR]$\f[R], \f[CR]*\f[R], and \f[CR]%\f[R].
Words count from \f[CR]0\f[R], the command.
\f[CR]!$\f[R], \f[CR]!\[ha]\f[R], and \f[CR]!*\f[R] select the last
argument, first argument, and every argument of the previous event.
A designator that selects a missing word is a bad word specifier.
.PP
.TS
tab(@);
